PVD("thailand_ndp_2023-2027",{"docs":["","Thailand 13th Plan 2023 27 THAI"],"s":{"1":[[1,"2","1","National Strategy Implementation Framework","The 13th National Economic and Social Development Plan (2023-2027) is a second-level plan that acts as a key mechanism to translate the National Strategy into implementation and serves as a framework for the formulation of third-level plans so as to enable relevant development partners to function in support of achieving the targets of the National Strategy within the expected timeframe.",""],[1,"3","2","National Resilience Preparedness and Structural Transformation Framework","Resiliency by focusing on three levels of development; namely, 1) 'Survival level' or 'Readiness' in resolving or eliminating existing limitations or weaknesses that cause hardships to people's lives or make the country vulnerable to internal and external changes as well as building preparedness for all levels of the society to cope with crises that might arise so that normalization can be quickly restored; 2) 'Sufficiency level' or 'Adjustment' of factors necessary to foster economic, social and environmental security from family level up to community and national levels.",""],[1,"7","1","Third-Level Action Plans for Government Projects","All of the four aforementioned second-level plans are key mechanisms for transforming national development directions in various dimensions under the National Strategy into action in the third-level plans, which is action plans to clearly identify the operations of government agencies' projects in accordance with their missions to ascertain the success of the second-level plans and the National Strategy in achieving their goals with coherence and integration at every level.",""],[1,"130","1","Integrated Plan Implementation and Coordination Mechanism","Achieving the goals of the 13th National Economic and Social Development Plan (2023- 2027) requires a systematically integrated cooperation of all sectors and implementation processes that: 1) translate the goals and strategic approaches of the plan into operations at the levels of measures, plans and projects with coherence; 2) genuinely reflect the development goals; 3) push for integrated, collaborative operations on common development missions shared by relevant agencies; and 4) facilitate co-operations with other sectors who are development parties in order to join forces in driving successful development outcomes.",""],[1,"130","1","Plan Budget Allocation Mechanism","Moreover, the success of the 13th Plan also relies on budget allocation mechanisms that support the plan's execution, together with monitoring and evaluation processes that are efficient and based on participation so as to support relevant agencies with useful information in their improvement of plans and processes to better respond to the goals.",""],[1,"130","4","Combined Multi-dimensional Planning Mechanisms","Combined multi-dimensional mechanisms - namely, the strategic mechanism, which focuses on creating factors that are important keys to the goals, as well as prioritizing operations according to their importance and urgency; the function-based mechanism, which is the fulfillment of official roles and responsibilities according to each agency's specialization; and the area-based mechanism, which translates development plans into action through the overall view at the regional and provincial levels with consideration of the area's socio-geographical conditions.",""],[1,"130","5","Cross-Sector Collaborative Operations Framework","Operation through co-operations from all sectors to gain acceptance and reduce limitations originated from operations by any single agency or solely by the public sector, with concentration on collaborative operations and common targets.",""],[1,"131","4","Integration of NESDP Implementation into Annual Budget Formulation","Integration of 13th NESDP implementation to annual fiscal expenditure budget formulation",""],[1,"131","18","13th Plan Outcome-Based Integration Mechanism","Implementation mechanisms consist of operations through two parallel mechanisms: namely, the Outcome-based Integration Mechanism, which aims at driving the 13th Plan to achieve target outcomes by integrating operations of relevant agencies in the public sector and by cooperating with other sectors;",""],[1,"131","18","13th Plan Function-Based and Area-Based Mechanism","and the Function-based Mechanism that includes the Area- based Mechanism, which operate along the regular missions of relevant agencies and at the area- level.",""],[1,"131","19","Outcome-Based Integration Mechanism","Outcome-based integration mechanism is a strategic operation mechanism that focuses on fostering the integration of operations by all relevant agencies in the public sector, connecting the operations with the incumbent national committees, and cultivating cooperation between the public sector and other sectors - the private sector, civil society, academic sector, population, and other development partners - in striving to achieve the goals stipulated in the milestones in a concrete manner.",""],[1,"131","20","Function-Based Multi-Stakeholder Plan Implementation Mechanism","Function-based mechanism puts an emphasis on connecting operations by relevant agencies according to their missions so that they can support the goals of the 13th Plan.",""],[1,"132","1","Area-Based Regional and Provincial Development Planning Mechanism","Area-based mechanism stresses on formulating regional development plans, provincial development plans, and various area development plans to ensure that they accommodate the implementation of the 13th Plan by designating development guidelines and operation plans and projects",""],[1,"132","2","Budget Mechanism for Plan Implementation","The budget mechanism is a major tool for steering the implementation of the 13th Plan towards outcome achievement in an efficient manner.",""],[1,"132","3","Integration of Plan Implementation into Annual Fiscal Budget Formulation","The integration of the 13th Plan implementation to the annual fiscal expenditure budget formulation so that the budget allocation system can support the achievement of the outcomes set in the 13th Plan's goals, by linking development priorities in each year under the 13th Plan to the fiscal budget allocation strategy.",""],[1,"132","4","Local Budget Administration and Management Support","The support for local agencies to administer and manage their budget with resiliency and in conformity to the 13th Plan in order to implement key development issues that are suitable for different contexts, potentials and demands of each local area.",""],[1,"132","5","Private Sector and Development Partner Investment Promotion Measures","The promotion of operations by various development partners by supporting the private sector and various development partners with potentials to invest in the manufacturing and service sectors targeted in the 13th Plan, including operations in development activities in which the private sector has expertise under designated measures and transparent inspection so that they can support the investment in its utmost effectiveness and efficiency.",""],[1,"132","6","Home-Temple-School Collaboration for Plan Implementation","encouraging the collaboration of the \"HTS\" (Home-Temple-School) - which includes communities, local administrative organizations, religious institutions, educational personnel, volunteers, voluntary social workers, and various development partners - to translate the strategies in the 13th Plan into collaborative actions for problem solving and development with participation of the local communities",""],[1,"132","6","Community and International Organization Partnership for Priority Development Issues","implementing the 13th Plan by promoting collaborations among communities and international organizations, particularly on development issues of high priority at the regional and sub-regional levels",""]],"2":[[1,"130","1","Participatory Monitoring and Evaluation System","Moreover, the success of the 13th Plan also relies on budget allocation mechanisms that support the plan's execution, together with monitoring and evaluation processes that are efficient and based on participation so as to support relevant agencies with useful information in their improvement of plans and processes to better respond to the goals.",""],[1,"130","2","PDCA Cycle for Systematic Operational Improvement","Adoption of PDCA cycle (Plan-Do-Check-Act cycle) as a framework to foster systematic operation processes that are continually developed and improved upon.",""],[1,"132","7","Plan Monitoring and Evaluation System","The monitoring and evaluation of the 13th Plan implementation covers monitoring and evaluation at the work plan and project levels, particularly work plans and projects with high priority to achieve the goals of each milestone, in order to forward feedbacks to relevant agencies and development partners for a review and improvement of the plans and operation process to ensure that the targets are reached.",""],[1,"132","7","Integrated Participatory Monitoring and Evaluation","Monitoring and evaluation at all levels must strive for integration and participation to",""],[1,"133","2","Progress Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","5.3.1 Progress Monitoring is the monitoring and evaluation while the projects are underway in order to inspect and monitor whether their operations align with the objectives, goals, and timeframes as well as examine whether there might be any obstacles that might delay or impede the operations from attaining specified outcomes within the designated timeframe.",""],[1,"133","3","National Outcome Evaluation and Public Consultation System","At this juncture, relevant agencies, both central and local agencies, shall report progress and outcomes of their action plans in the national monitoring and evaluation system.",""]],"3":[[1,"20","1","Public Sector Administrative Transformation for Social Partnership","The public sector is therefore compelled to acknowledge a need to transform its administration and management so that it can connect with, and provide opportunities for, all sectors in the society, by inviting them to become partners in the national development effort to ensure greater participation and efficiency and to consequently restore trust in the public sector.",""],[1,"20","2","Public Administration Development for Service Quality and Efficiency","public administration development to strengthen the institutional capital during the 13th Plan will focus on enhancing public administration's quality and efficiency in order to promptly and substantially respond to people's demands.",""],[1,"20","2","Integrated Central-Local Government Coordination System","Connections between the central agency and local agencies shall be forged in an integrated system with good governance to maintain social stability and bolster the country's institutional capital.",""],[1,"20","3","Participatory Public Policy and Administration Processes","At the same time, it must resort to information and participatory processes in formulating public policies and in public administration and management to keep up with changes and to respond promptly to changing situations, with the ultimate goal of enhancing the country's capability in dealing with changes and risks in a new global context.",""],[1,"22","7","Public Administration Restructuring for Timely and Efficient Response","Restructuring the public administrative system to be able to respond to changes in socioeconomic and technological contexts in a timely and efficient manner and with good governance.",""],[1,"124","2","Public Service Improvement and Administrative Reform","Areas for public sector improvement to keep up with changes and strengthen the public sector's capacity are: 1) Making public services responsive, convenient, and cost-effective to the general public and businesses by increasing the quality of services and allowing participations by other sectors; 2) Adjusting public sector administration as well as restructuring the public sector to ensure flexibility, connectivity, openness and efficiency to support changes and the country's development; 3) Adopting digital transformation and transitioning to e-government capable of utilizing data to inform the country's development and administration; 4) Building a public sector administrative system which supports capacity building to possess necessary skills in providing e-government services as well as revising laws, regulations and government measures to support the country's development.",""],[1,"124","8","Public Sector Results-Based Working Culture Reform","A public sector shift to results based working culture and public interests, which conveniently, responsively and transparently respond to people's needs;",""],[1,"124","8","Public Sector Downsizing and Adaptation Reform","and 2) A more adaptable and smaller public sector.",""],[1,"126","10","Public Sector Administration Restructuring and Flexibility Reform","Adjusting public sector administration as well as restructuring the public sector to ensure flexibility. connectivity, openness & efficiency in order to keep up with changes and support country's development",""],[1,"126","15","Public Sector Role Review and Decentralization of Authority","Urgently reviewing public sector's roles & decentralizing authority",""],[1,"126","16","Public Sector Human Resource Management Reform","Revising public sector's human resource management system to retain & attract high-capability personnel",""],[1,"127","1","Public Service Outsourcing and Service Innovation Mechanism","Terminating services that can be outsourced to other sectors.",""],[1,"127","3","Public Sector Role Review and Decentralization Reform","Urgently reviewing the public sector's roles as well as decentralizing authority.",""],[1,"128","3","Public Sector Human Resources Management Reform","Sub-strategy 4.1 Revising the public sector's human resources management system to retain and attract high-capability personnel in order to help propel the country's development.",""]],"4":[[1,"20","3","Legal Reform for National Development","At the same time, outdated and unnecessary laws shall be revoked while laws and regulations supporting national development for future growth shall be formulated so that Thailand will have a modern, efficient, and responsive public sector that meets people's expectations and can truly contribute to Thailand's transformation.",""],[1,"128","4","Legal Reform and Law Repeal Initiative","Abolishing unnecessary laws and enacting new laws conducive to the country's development, as well as enhancing the efficiency of the justice system.",""],[1,"128","4","Public Sector Facilitation Reform","Adjusting the public sector's role to become a facilitator that supports the private sector and the public in development missions.",""],[1,"128","4","Results-Based Law Reform for Well-Being and Competitiveness","Reforming and enacting laws with measurable goals focusing on the well-being of Thai people and the enhancement of the country's competitiveness.",""],[1,"128","4","Justice System Efficiency Improvement","Improving the efficiency of the justice system.",""],[1,"128","4","Cross-Organizational Work Integration Initiative","Encouraging cross- organizational work integration to ensure speedy work processes, fairness to the affected parties, and convenience for the broad public.",""],[1,"128","4","Urgent Review of Outdated Laws","Designating a responsible agency to urgently revise outdated laws.",""],[1,"128","4","Regulatory Repeal of Obstructive Laws","Revoke unnecessary, redundant or obstructive laws which hinder public administration or adaptation, especially laws that obstruct the transition into e-government at all levels and laws that discourage the monitoring of government functions.",""],[1,"128","4","National Legal Database Development","Developing and integrating a secure, convenient, easy-access and easy-to-understand national legal database according to the nature of the entities accessing the database.",""]],"5":[[1,"127","4","Public Sector Transparency and Information Disclosure Initiative","Enabling a disclosure of information through various technologies and allowing the public to access and engage in delivering information, facts and opinions, and monitoring government performance through multiple communication channels.",""],[1,"132","6","Stakeholder Consultation Platforms and Channels","creating platforms or channels for all partners to express their ideas and opinions",""]],"6":[[1,"20","3","Digital Government Transformation","The public sector therefore must expedite the development of institutional mechanisms to support a transformation into digital government by deploying technology in providing public services to ensure speed, convenience and efficiency.",""],[1,"20","3","Public Sector Resilience and Service Digitization","Besides, the public sector must review its role and operational processes with an emphasis on developing its capacity for resilience, connectivity and openness, as well as committing to the digitization of information and services to give people and businesses convenient, speedy and economical access, while guaranteeing that the public sector's services are of good quality and responsive to the demands and expectations of people and all sectors in an efficient, equitable and timely manner.",""],[1,"20","3","Digital Public Service Skills Development","To achieve these goals, the public sector's human resources administration and management system needs to be modified to place a stress on equipping personnel with the necessary skills for digital public services.",""],[1,"22","7","Digital Transformation Enabling Infrastructure and Institutions","Developing basic infrastructure and institutional mechanisms conducive to digital transformation.",""],[1,"126","12","Public Management System Reform for E-Government Skills","Strategy 4 Building public management system that supports turnover & development of personnel to ensure necessary skills for e-government services.",""],[1,"127","2","Public Administrative Process Reform and E-Government Integration","Sub-strategy 1.2 Revising public administrative processes together with developing comprehensive e-government services.",""],[1,"127","4","Integrated Information Management for Collaborative Decision-Making","Integrating information management tasks and utilizing acquired information in a decision-making process for collaborative development and problem solving in order to diminish corruption.",""],[1,"127","5","Government Data Digitization and Integration Initiative","Sub-strategy 3.1 Digitizing all government data.",""],[1,"128","1","Public Sector Policy Data Integration System","Prioritizing and urgently developing a system to integrate data essential for the public sector's policy-related decision-making processes in overall resource management.",""],[1,"128","2","Public Sector Work Process Digitization","Digitizing all public sector's work processes.",""]],"7":[[1,"12","2","Manufacturing Sector Transformation into an Innovation-Driven Economy","Thailand's economic development during the 13th Plan needs to expedite a transformation of the manufacturing sector into an innovation-driven economy that aims for sustainable development.",""],[1,"12","2","Product and Service Quality Enhancement Initiative","This ambition can be accomplished by emphasizing product and service quality enhancement to create higher value and by ensuring the fair and practical distribution of economic benefits to all relevant domestic sectors.",""],[1,"12","2","National Economic Restructuring and Multilevel Policy Cascade","diverse approaches for national economic restructuring need to be cascaded into multilevel policies and plans that support the transformation of key potential sectors to become industries and services of the future as the forthcoming drivers for economic growth.",""],[1,"12","2","Technology-Driven Productivity Upgrade for Potential Industries","Thailand needs to boost the growth of industries with potentials and advantages by integrating technology to rapidly improve their overall productivity for high-value products and services.",""],[1,"12","2","Research and Development Investment for Innovation and Intellectual Property","This requires investment in research and development to advance existing knowledge and foster innovation that will lead to the creation of Thai intellectual property with an emphasis on value and sustainability.",""],[1,"12","2","Development of Future Industries Aligned with Global Market Trends","Thailand should also focus on developing new industries of the future that align with global market trends so as to offset the declining domestic purchasing power.",""],[1,"12","2","Enabling Ecosystem for Fair Competition and Global Value Chain Integration","Achieving this objective requires efforts to enhance the quality of production factors, building an enabling ecosystem for fair competition, upgrading links to the global value chain, and maximizing the utilization of the existing infrastructure, incorporating technology and fostering innovation to improve labor productivity to correspond to the target of transforming into the future-oriented and high-value creation industry and service sectors.",""],[1,"22","3","Manufacturing and Service Sector Innovation Upgrade","Enhancing competitiveness of key manufacturing and service sectors by stimulating value added enhancement through innovation, technology and creativity that corresponds to the development of a modern society and is environmental-friendly.",""],[1,"22","3","Innovation, Trade and Investment Enabling Ecosystem Development","Developing and promoting enabling ecosystem that supports innovation, trade and investment.",""],[1,"62","4","Next-Generation Industry and Services Development","Next-generation industry and service sectors focusing on developing and transitioning Thailand's target industries into next- generation industries as a pillar of the country's economy, as well as building an enabling ecosystem for the development of industries and services;",""],[1,"69","2","Next-Generation Industrial and Service Development","Competitiveness enhancement through next-generation industrial and service development with a focus on advancing Thailand's target industries into the industries of the future that will become the pillars of the Thai economy, creating an enabling environment conducive to industrial and service development and developing sufficient, high quality, comprehensive and affordable technological infrastructure",""],[1,"71","24","Electrical and Electronics Industry Upgrade to ODM and Modern Manufacturing Innovation","Supporting enterprises in electrical and electronicsindustry to shift from CEM to ODMand adopt modem manufacturing innovation",""],[1,"72","5","Electrical and Electronics Industry Upgrading Support","Supporting enterprises in the electrical and electronics industry to shift from original equipment manufacturers (OEM) to original design manufacturers (ODM), as well as adopting modern manufacturing innovations to transition into Industry 4.0 and a green electronics industry through fiscal and financial tools as well as other innovation promotion policies.",""],[1,"72","6","Smart Electronics Industry Upgrading Strategy","Encouraging enterprises in the smart electronics industry to adjust their development model in order to become ASEAN's key manufacturers of smart electronic gadgets and parts, focusing on the production of sought-after and high-value key parts in the global supply chain and a shift to advanced electronics industry, such as the manufacturing of supercapacitors, optoelectronics, and microelectronics.",""],[1,"72","6","Domestic Materials Procurement Promotion","Encouraging the industrial sector to use materials from domestic manufacturers.",""],[1,"72","8","Advanced Technology R&D Investment Promotion","Promoting investment in research and development of advanced technologies in the smart electrical and electronics industry as well as the development of product",""],[1,"73","1","Incentives for Smart Electronic Manufacturing Start-ups","Providing incentives for starting new businesses to manufacture smart electronic products and parts.",""],[1,"73","3","Foreign Investment Promotion and Knowledge Transfer Incentives","Attracting and encouraging foreign investment by collaborating with Thai businesses or joint ventures, together with giving privileges for investors that encourage or press for specialist partners to transfer knowledge and expertise to Thai enterprises with a focus on upstream industries with advanced manufacturing technology, which are the basis for the smart electronics industry.",""],[1,"73","8","Digital Industry and Services Investment Promotion","Promoting investment and domestic research and development in the digital industry and services to meet the needs of domestic and ASEAN markets.",""],[1,"73","8","Tech Company and Digital Ecosystem Development","Attracting and developing tech companies of all sizes, ranging from startups to global corporations, and building a digital ecosystem to increase opportunities for Thai tech businesses.",""],[1,"73","8","Tax Incentives for Digital Startups","Offering appropriate privileges, such as tax measures, to boost investment in digital startups.",""],[1,"74","4","Fiscal and Financial Incentives for Smart Electronics and Digital Industry Innovation","Advocating for the use of appropriate fiscal and financial policy tools that correspond to each industry's context in order to stimulate investment in research and development and innovation as well as boost competitiveness of the smart electronics and digital industries and services, such as tax reduction for importation of digital technology and a verification, monitoring and protection system for consumers in the digital industry.",""],[1,"98","6","Next-Generation Industry and Services Competitiveness Enhancement","Competitiveness enhancement in next-generation industry and services with the goal of driving the country's development with innovation and technology of the future, together with building enabling ecosystems and supporting the sustainable development of industries and services;",""]],"8":[[1,"15","4","SME Competitiveness and Sustainable Growth Support","an emphasis should be placed on the development of SMEs' competitiveness potential and sustainable growth by creating an",""],[1,"16","1","SME Competitiveness and Global Value Chain Integration Support","providing technological support, accessible financial mechanism to cover all capital sources, upgrading product and service standards, as well as connecting Thai SMEs to the global value chain network.",""],[1,"22","3","Local Economy and Small Entrepreneur Value Chain Integration","Linking local economy and small entrepreneurs with the production value chain and target services.",""],[1,"76","2","SME Competitiveness and Global Value Chain Integration","Target 1: Restructuring the manufacturing and service sectors towards an innovation-based economy by developing and enhancing competitiveness of SMEs in every sector as well as enabling SMEs to connect to the global value chain with an enabling ecosystem appropriate for each type and sector of business",""],[1,"76","2","Fair Competition and Opportunity Promotion for SMEs","Target 3: Creating a society of opportunities and fairness by reducing disparities in income, wealth and business competitiveness and by promoting fair and open competition among SMEs to compete sustainably",""],[1,"78","34","SME Digital Technology and Automation Incentive Scheme","Offering benefit & incentives to encourage SMEs to inwest in and utilize digital technology, machinery and automation in mangement, and tr unharicu manufacturing & survice efficiency",""],[1,"80","4","SME Competitiveness and Sustainable Business Preparedness Support","Building SMEs' preparedness for coping with intense and fast-changing competition in the modern market, as well as for sustainable business operations, taking into consideration the environment, society and good governance, in order to achieve international competitiveness.",""],[1,"80","5","SME Digital Technology and Automation Incentive Scheme","Offering benefits and incentives to encourage SMEs to invest in and utilize digital technology, machinery and automation in management, and to enhance manufacturing and service efficiency.",""],[1,"80","7","SME Supply Chain Collaboration and Business Alliance Programme","Promoting network building and business alliances.",""],[1,"80","7","Large Corporation Support for SME Integration","Pairing and encouraging large corporations with potentials to provide comprehensive assistance to SMEs in the supply chain.",""],[1,"80","7","SME Business Forum and Experience Exchange Initiative","Organizing forums for exchanging business ideas and experiences to develop sustainable collaboration among SMEs at all levels.",""],[1,"86","1","Target Industry and SME Supply Chain Integration","Determining target industries in the areas where the new economy bases are located in line with local potentials.",""]],"9":[[1,"75","2","SME Capacity-Building Training Programme","The government and relevant agencies have continuously promoted and supported SME development; for example, building capacity for business operations through trainings on entrepreneurial attitudes and skills, financial literacy, manufacturing and services, product and packaging development, and marketing.",""],[1,"76","2","Human Capital Development for the New Global Era","Target 2: Developing human capital for the new global era by equipping Thai people with skills and traits that fit the modern world in terms of knowledge, behavioral skills, and manners according to the norms of society",""],[1,"78","31","Business Development Services Expansion for SMEs","Expanding business development services to meet specific needs of SMEa",""],[1,"78","31","SME Referral System Development","developing a referral system",""],[1,"79","3","Digital Infrastructure and Standard Systems Support for SMEs","Developing digital infrastructure and standard systems accessible to SMEs at low costs by providing partial subsidies for the use of technology and basic software in boosting business efficiency and standards, especially in analysis, testing and certification.",""],[1,"79","3","Specialized SME Incubation Center Expansion","Expanding services of incubation centers specializing in specific businesses to cover the development and enhancement of SMEs' products and services to achieve quality, innovativeness, and international competitiveness.",""],[1,"79","6","Online SME Data and Knowledge Repository Platform","Sub-strategy 2.3 Transforming data and knowledge repository for SMEs into an online system as well as comprehensive e-services.",""],[1,"80","4","Basic Business Knowledge and Skills Development for Youth and Entrepreneurs","Fostering basic business knowledge especially knowledge and skills of the youth and entrepreneurs regarding digital, finance, new marketing, export market acquisition, business models, creative economy, exploitation of cultural capital, as well as other in-depth knowledge and skills as needed for specific sectors and types of business.",""],[1,"80","8","SME Business Development Services Expansion","Expanding business development services that reach specific needs of SMEs",""],[1,"80","8","SME Business Development Referral System","developing a referral system by expanding on the government's coupon initiative",""],[1,"80","8","Private Provider Registration and Capacity Assessment System","Developing registration and capacity assessment systems for private providers of business development services",""],[1,"120","4","Entrepreneur Support in Manufacturing and Services Areas","Fostering entrepreneurs who work with the manufacturing and service sectors in an area.",""],[1,"121","8","Entrepreneur Knowledge and Skills Development Programme","Encouraging entrepreneurs to acquire comprehensive knowledge necessary for modern businesses.",""],[1,"121","8","Entrepreneurial Mindset and Innovation Awareness Initiative","Fostering new beliefs that bring about awareness and gaining new knowledge.",""],[1,"121","8","Business Data Analytics and Risk Management Training","Strengthening skills in data application and analysis in order to inform business planning and risk management through convenient, concise and time-effective learning formats in both formal and informal education responsive to each individual's needs, through learning technologies.",""],[1,"121","8","Entrepreneur Learning Community Network","Building a community of entrepreneurs to share learning and inspirations for change.",""],[1,"121","9","Entrepreneur Innovation Sandbox and Funding Support","Encouraging entrepreneurs to innovate to support the value creation in future industries through establishing sandboxes for entrepreneurs to compete and test concepts, promoting investments for innovation development, as well as business matching and funding.",""]],"10":[[1,"120","1","Research Network and Center of Excellence Linkage Initiative","Linking research systems and mechanisms of research networks with domestic and international centers for excellence to embrace world-class researchers and technologists in developing and expanding on research on national development.",""],[1,"120","1","University-Startup Innovation Holding Company Collaboration","Promoting collaborations among higher education institutions, researchers and startups in the form of holding companies to develop innovation-based businesses.",""],[1,"120","1","Higher Education-SME Research Collaboration Programme","Encouraging higher education institutions to conduct research with SMEs in the manufacturing and service sectors to facilitate a transition towards innovation-based economy and boost the country's competitiveness.",""]],"11":[[1,"82","6","Special Economic Zone Infrastructure Readiness and Investment Facilitation Reform","Therefore, the focus of development should be on ensuring infrastructure readiness as well as reviewing and revising investment promotion and facilitation measures to accommodate investments.",""]],"12":[[1,"61","2","Transport Infrastructure Investment for Regional Connectivity","Thailand needs to increase investment by no less than 600 billion baht to escape from the middle-income trap, as well as urgently use the surplus from its economic expansion to reduce inequalities through investments in transport infrastructure to connect with neighboring countries, economic decentralization from Bangkok to regions throughout the country, and an increased private sector role in services to ensure maximum benefits and efficiency from investments in transport projects.",""],[1,"65","6","Special Development Zone Infrastructure and Cross-Border Connectivity Investment","Investing in infrastructure and developing supporting factors to promote special development zones and areas with current and future potentials, including transport infrastructure, logistics services and networks along key routes and links with neighboring countries, cross-border investment and trade facilities, ports and land bridges in the Southern Economic Corridor to turn Thailand into a strategic gateway.",""],[1,"65","6","Tourism and Services Infrastructure Development in High-Potential Provinces","Investing in, and developing, infrastructure to enhance and accommodate tourism and services in provinces with potentials, such as connecting tourism in the Andaman Sea, which include Phuket, Krabi, Phang- nga, Trang and Satun provinces, so as to become one of the world's top five cruise destinations.",""],[1,"65","7","Seamless Multimodal Transportation and Logistics System Development","Developing a seamless multimodal transportation and logistics system at the regional, sub-regional and cross-border levels.",""],[1,"66","1","Rail Network Development and Regional Rail Linkage Programme","Continuously giving importance to the rail system and turning it into Thailand's main transport network with linkages to regional and sub-regional logistics networks in order to minimize logistics costs.",""],[1,"66","1","Thailand-Laos-China Rail Connectivity Support","Supporting rail connections between Thailand, Laos and China at Nongkhai and Chiangrai provinces as well as facilitating rail connections between local economic zones in the Northern, Northeastern, Central and Eastern regions and China and GMS countries.",""],[1,"66","2","River and Coastal Transport Capacity Enhancement","Building and enhancing the capacity of river and coastal transport, focusing on convenient, modern and safe transport along key rivers, including the Chao Phraya, Nan and Pasak rivers, and particularly along the Chao Phraya to Laem Chabang Port.",""],[1,"66","2","Waterway Development for Domestic and International Transport","Developing waterways for economic purposes to boost the effectiveness of domestic and international transport.",""],[1,"66","3","Logistics Management Efficiency Improvement","Improving basic infrastructure management systems by, for example, adopting modern technologies, enhancing service systems, developing software, and relaxing relevant rules and regulations.",""],[1,"66","4","Logistics Service Center Investment Development","Encouraging investment in building logistics service centers, which includes container yards or inland container depots, dry ports, and loading-unloading docks, with an emphasis on integrating investment plans into key strategic transport routes to enable connections with GMS countries, China and ASEAN.",""],[1,"66","4","Rail Freight Modal Shift Pricing Policy","Setting compelling service rates to motivate a shift in transport modes to rail system.",""],[1,"66","5","Private Sector Infrastructure Investment Promotion","Encouraging more private sector investment in infrastructure with transparency, accountability and clear evaluation of efficiency and success.",""],[1,"66","5","Expanded Private Sector Service Provision","Allowing operators in the trade, investment and service sectors to have more roles in service provision.",""],[1,"66","6","Modern Technology Adoption in Production","Expediting the adoption of modern technologies in production in the industrial, service, and logistics sectors, particularly in terms of a shift to automate production and prompt exploitation of technological advancement.",""]],"13":[[1,"88","2","Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Development","Developing transport and logistics infrastructure to ensure safe, convenient and effective transportation and transports of goods and raw materials.",""],[1,"88","2","Modern Inclusive Telecommunications Infrastructure Development","Developing telecommunication infrastructure which is modern, inclusive, and of high quality.",""],[1,"88","2","Science, Technology and Innovation Infrastructure Development","Developing scientific, technology and innovation infrastructure to support research and development for commercialization.",""],[1,"88","2","Digital Technology Adoption and Business Transformation Support","Promoting the adoption of digital technologies to create value add as well as encouraging entrepreneurs to carry out digital transformation in business operations.",""],[1,"88","2","Urban Tourism Infrastructure and Facilities Development","Developing the city's infrastructure and facilities to accommodate tourism and related services.",""],[1,"89","1","Mass Transit System Development","These include an investment plan to revive a city's economy in specific development area or high value economic zones and plan to invest in, and develop, a mass transit system to connect and provide convenience to all groups of the population.",""]],"14":[[1,"12","3","Quality and Sustainable Tourism Transformation","2) Transforming the tourism sector, Thailand's key service sector, into quality-focused and sustainable tourism by promoting quality, value, and sustainability over quantity, and creating added value for services that align with the modern market's directions and trends;",""],[1,"39","25","Happy Model Tourism Development","Develo ping \"Happy Model \" to urism per the revised Natio nal Eco no mic Reform Plan.",""],[1,"39","25","Knowledge and Data Support for High-Quality Tourism Products","Supporting collection of knowledge & data on geographical, biological and cultural diversity as well as local lifestyles with unique identities to create value added in a form of products and services for high-quality tourism.",""],[1,"39","34","Quality Tourism Development Initiative","Promoting development of quality tourism with high growth potentials, such as 1) \"Shopping Paradis'e initiative: by promoting national souvenir groups, tax reduction policy for some luxury goods, dutyfree areas to expand on the Phuket Sandbox) Maritime tourism e.g. pleasure cruises, yachts and river cruises by setting clear development plan with the private sector; 3) Man-made tourist attractions, business travels and MICE tourism to attract high purchasingower groups.",""],[1,"40","1","Happy Model Tourism Development","Sub-strategy 1.1 Developing \"Happy Model\" tourism as per the revised National Economic Reform Plan.",""],[1,"40","2","Shopping Paradise Tourism Initiative","1) \"Shopping Paradise\" initiative: by encouraging the launch of national souvenir groups as well as tax reduction policies for importing certain classes of luxury goods, establishing duty-free areas as an extension of the Phuket Sandbox to stimulate spending and revenue distribution to small entrepreneurs;",""],[1,"40","2","Maritime Tourism Development Plan","2) Maritime tourism including pleasure cruises, yachts and river cruises: by formulating a clear development plan in collaboration with the private sector to identify locations for marinas both as home ports and transit ports, for cruises in areas with potentials along the Gulf of Thailand and the Andaman Sea such as Pattaya and Phuket, together with creating tourist spots in connection with the marinas to substantially stimulate private investment and revenue distribution;",""],[1,"40","2","Man-Made Attractions and MICE Tourism Promotion","3) Promoting man-made tourist attractions, business travel and MICE (Meetings, Incentives, Conferences and Exhibitions) tourism to boost domestic and international investments, business travels as well as other travel styles for high purchasing-power groups such as senior citizens, retirees, long-term visitors, and digital nomads.",""],[1,"40","3","Creative Economy and Tourism Innovation Support","Encouraging businesses and startups to adopt creative economy concepts, cultural uniqueness and technology and innovation in developing and creating value add to tourism.",""],[1,"40","3","Tourism Soft Power Promotion Initiative","Promoting soft power as a driving force for tourism.",""],[1,"40","3","Tourism Research, Digital Services, and Innovation Support","Supporting research and development as well as the use of information technology and innovation in enhancing services, marketing and ease of travel.",""]],"15":[[1,"39","6","Tourism Sector Restructuring for Domestic Travelers","To restructure tourism sector to lean towards domestic travelers & to improve economic opportunity distribution",""],[1,"39","35","Community-Based Tourism and Secondary City Tourism Support","Supporting communityased tourism and tourism in secondary cities with special attention on development based on biological and cultural divers Establishing network and providing funding to incubate communities into social enterprises and startups to improve revenue distribution.",""],[1,"39","35","Community Social Enterprise and Startup Incubation Support","Establishing network and providing funding to incubate communities into social enterprises and startups to improve revenue distribution.",""],[1,"39","40","Private Sector Collaboration for Community Tourism Development","Promoting private sector collaboration & engagement in developing community tourist destinations & determining directions on local tourism development and maintenance of tourist destinations.",""],[1,"40","4","Development of Quality Tourist Attractions and Services in Secondary Destinations","Developing quality tourist attractions and services at high- potential secondary destinations",""],[1,"40","4","Tourist Route Diversification and Domestic Travel Promotion","spreading a variety of tourist routes thoroughly to boost domestic travel and attract quality tourists from around the world to local tourist destinations",""],[1,"40","4","Local Tourism Clustering Support","Supporting clustering according to local potentials.",""],[1,"40","5","Community-Based Tourism Support Programme","Supporting community-based tourism and tourism in secondary cities with special attention on development based on biological and cultural diversity.",""],[1,"40","5","Ecotourism Knowledge Development Initiative","Building ecotourism knowledge.",""],[1,"40","5","Environmental Management Systems for Tourist Destinations","Developing environmental management systems at tourist destinations to promote community and cultural protection.",""],[1,"40","5","Community Enterprise and Startup Incubation Network","Establishing networks and providing funding to incubate communities into social enterprises and startups to improve revenue distribution.",""],[1,"40","6","Private Sector Collaboration for Community Tourism Development","Promoting private sector collaboration and engagement in developing community tourist destinations and in determining directions on local tourism development, security and safety, and maintenance of tourist destinations to ensure good conditions.",""],[1,"101","7","Community Income Generation from Biological and Cultural Diversity","Encouraging income generation from natural resources and cultural conservation.",""],[1,"101","7","Ecotourism Capacity Building for Local Communities","Boosting the capacity of local populations by equipping them with ecotourism knowledge and awareness of local identity and cultural heritage.",""],[1,"101","7","Environmental Management Systems for Tourist Destinations","Developing environmental management systems at tourist destinations.",""]],"16":[[1,"39","27","Sustainable Tourism Area Management Systems","developing tourist area management systems in line with ecosystem's capacity",""],[1,"39","27","Eco-friendly Enterprise Support for Tourism","supporting eco - friendly enterprises",""],[1,"39","27","Low-Emission Tourism Transport Measures","Promoting use of electric vehicles and other measures to reduce GHG emission in the tourism industry",""],[1,"41","1","Sustainable Tourist Area Management Systems","developing tourist area management systems in line with the ecosystem's capacity",""],[1,"41","1","Eco-friendly Tourism Enterprise Support","supporting eco-friendly enterprises",""],[1,"41","1","Electric Vehicle Promotion in Tourism","Promoting the use of electric vehicles and other measures to reduce greenhouse gas (GHG) emission in the tourism industry.",""],[1,"41","7","Responsible Tourism Guidelines at Tourist Destinations","Sub-strategy 4.3 Establishing appropriate guidelines on responsible tourism at tourist destinations for businesses, personnel, and tourists.",""]],"17":[[1,"58","9","National Health Database Development","Initiating a national health database by forging collaboration among relevant agencies through mutual agreement to link together basic data from public agencies on a common interoperable digital platform while taking into account personal data protection, such as data on morbidity and mortality, incapacitation, health security, research and innovation, number of healthcare workers and experts produced and currently in service for analyzing and expanding on the acquired data for service management and the planning of future workforce.",""],[1,"59","2","Integrated Epidemic Surveillance and Emergency Response System","Restructuring and unifying the epidemics surveillance and management system.",""],[1,"59","3","Integrated Health and Environmental Surveillance System","Developing integrated health and environmental surveillance mechanisms and data systems.",""],[1,"59","4","Emergency Public Health Preparedness System","Establishing an emergency preparedness system to ensure public health security.",""]],"18":[[1,"13","1","Medical and Wellness Hub Development Programme","Propelling Thailand to become a high-value medical and wellness hub by producing more medical and healthcare personnel, upgrading standards, and supporting the utilization of advancements from cutting-edge research and technology in treatment processes and healthcare services as a means to create added value and to upgrade the level of services based on innovative and advanced technology",""],[1,"52","5","Comprehensive Healthcare Industry Development","Milestone No. 4 is also consistent with the National Strategy in the area of Competitiveness Enhancement under the goal \"Thailand's national competitiveness is increased\" through the designation of the comprehensive healthcare industry as a service industry of the future; leveraging Thailand's medical expertise to build associated industries related to the development of medical industry and services; using new technologies to raise the quality of medical services to international standards; and linking the industry with medical tourism.",""],[1,"54","21","Private Sector Medical Services Innovation and Regulation Support","Encouraging private sector to enhance medical services based on innovations & advanced technology through govemment standards, supports, and regulatory measures",""],[1,"55","1","Private Sector Medical Services Innovation Support and Regulation","Encouraging the private sector to enhance medical services based on innovations and advanced technologies through government standards, supports, and regulatory measures.",""],[1,"55","2","Precision and Personalized Healthcare Development","Enhancing medical services with a focus on precision medicine, predictive medicine and personalized healthcare.",""],[1,"55","2","Target Group Health Database Development","Developing target group databases to enable individualized treatment and care as well as gene and stem cell therapies.",""],[1,"55","2","Evidence-Based Medical Services and Anti-Ageing Medicine Support","Utilizing healthcare services to support evidence-based medical services, including anti-ageing medicine.",""],[1,"55","3","Advanced Medical Services Quality Control System","Developing a quality control system to regulate quality standards in advanced medical services, taking into consideration all aspects of impacts.",""],[1,"56","2","New Wellness Services Development","Sub-strategy 2.3 Developing new wellness services to ensure well-being in an ageing society.",""],[1,"56","2","Digital Community Wellness Spaces","Accommodating spaces for digital communities for well-being based on service and product innovations appropriate for new normal lifestyles, such as telemedicine and appropriate changes in behaviors and lifestyles through food therapy and mental therapy in the form of meditation.",""],[1,"56","2","Universal Architecture Healthcare Infrastructure","Developing infrastructure with universal architecture to support long-term healthcare services.",""],[1,"56","2","Elderly Residential and Recreation Areas","Establishing residential areas for the elderly as well as areas for sports and exercises to encourage longer stays among the active elderly and work-and-travel visitors.",""],[1,"58","7","Digital and ICT System for Medical Services","Sub-strategy 5.3 Developing a digital and ICT system to support medical services.",""],[1,"58","8","Digital Health Technology Adoption","Encouraging the use of digital technology to increase efficiency, reduce workloads, and address personnel shortages, such as artificial intelligence for basic screening and telemedicine.",""],[1,"58","8","Expansion of Digital Infrastructure Coverage","Expanding the coverage of digital infrastructure.",""],[1,"58","8","Medical Technology Regulation and Evaluation Framework","Revising relevant rules and regulations together with formulating mechanisms and guidelines to evaluate the use of medical technology and to avoid possible negative impacts.",""]],"19":[[1,"104","4","Household Alternative Energy and Energy-Saving Innovation Promotion","Sub-strategy 5.4 Advocating for alternative energy and energy saving innovation for households.",""],[1,"104","4","Alternative Energy Infrastructure and Data Systems Development","Developing basic infrastructure and data systems for the management, production and use of alternative energy.",""],[1,"104","4","Alternative Energy Research and Development Support","Supporting research and development of efficient technologies in alternative energy.",""],[1,"104","4","Affordable Energy-Saving Innovation Promotion","Promoting affordable energy-saving innovations.",""],[1,"104","4","Public Awareness Campaign on Efficient Energy Consumption","Raising awareness and disseminating information to encourage the public to choose technologies with efficient energy consumption and long-term cost reductions.",""]],"20":[[1,"121","11","Learning Cities and Creative Spaces Promotion","Promoting all sectors in society to develop learning cities, learning facilities and diverse creative spaces both physically and virtually.",""],[1,"122","1","Quality Learning Facilities and Creative Spaces Development","build and develop quality learning facilities and creative spaces that offer up-to-date content in line with the needs of all groups of learners, together with having wide coverage and high accessibility both in physical and virtual spaces",""]],"21":[[1,"102","4","Forest Plantation Incentive Mechanisms","Formulating systems and mechanisms to encourage forest plantations to boost communities' economy.",""],[1,"102","4","Reforestation of Degraded and Abandoned Areas","Building mechanisms to inspire the planting of new forests in degraded or abandoned areas.",""],[1,"102","4","Tree Bank Initiative","Implementing the Tree Bank initiative.",""],[1,"102","4","Timber Traceability System","Developing a tracing system for timber production, processing, and trade throughout the production chain.",""],[1,"102","4","Tree Variety Research and Timber Innovation Support","Supporting research and development in viable tree varieties and innovation to create value add from timber.",""],[1,"102","4","Economic Tree Planting Incentives","Incentivizing the planting of trees with economic value.",""],[1,"102","5","Natural Resource Value Evaluation for Efficient Management","Conducting a value evaluation of natural resources to increase the efficiency of natural resources management.",""],[1,"102","7","Sustainable Natural Resource Management Sub-Strategy","Sub-strategy 3.3 Managing economic activities within the capacity of natural resources in the area.",""]],"23":[[1,"87","2","Ecological Corridor Connectivity Between Cities","Encouraging connecting ecological areas between cities.",""],[1,"89","1","Waste and Wastewater Management Improvement","extensive management of waste and wastewater with appropriate technology, safety, and preparedness against all forms of disasters.",""],[1,"89","1","Urban Learning Zone for Innovation and Problem Solving","Establishing an urban learning zone to incubate innovation in area development management and collective problem solving, which might lead to sandboxes to test new ideas such as the disclosure and sharing of data, the forging of local knowledge, understanding and awareness on health and hygiene, food production systems, and healthy consumption behaviors through a network of community volunteers, such as Village Health Volunteers (VHV), for preparation against epidemics and emerging diseases.",""],[1,"89","2","Local Government Financial Agility and Revenue Reform","Revising regulations to allow local governments to have financial agility and ability to generate incomes and raise funds from local populations.",""]],"24":[[1,"33","2","Sustainable Agricultural Practices Promotion","Promoting sustainable agriculture with consideration to environmental impacts and nature-based development through the sustainable protection, management and rehabilitation of nature/ecosystems in order to improve the quality of people's lives and benefit biological diversity, particularly through sustainable agricultural practices such as reforestation, agroforestry, elimination of open burning, legal fisheries and good labor practices.",""],[1,"33","3","Support for Eco-friendly High Value-added Agricultural Inputs","Sub-strategy 3.2 Supporting necessary inputs to ensure further adoption of eco- friendly, high value-added agricultural models.",""],[1,"33","7","Watershed and Economic Forest Expansion Initiative","Advocating for an expansion of watershed forests/economic forests to generate income in areas inappropriate for farming, as well as increasing natural water volume for adequate use by the entire system.",""],[1,"33","8","Irrigation and Water Distribution Rehabilitation and Water Source Management","Urgently developing and rehabilitating irrigation and water distribution systems in irrigated areas, together with developing and managing water sources outside irrigated areas and community water sources, as well as proper sediment management to increase the water retention capability of reservoirs.",""],[1,"33","9","Reservoir Sediment Management and Erosion Control","Sub-strategy 4.3 Ensuring appropriate sediment management to increase the water retention capability of reservoirs.",""],[1,"33","10","Systematic and Balanced Water Utilization Planning","Managing and planning for systematic and balanced water utilization, as well as establishing and disseminating knowledge on efficient water utilization, such as a reuse of water.",""]],"25":[[1,"86","1","Regional Economic Corridor Development","Developing the regions to become the country's key economic bases in accordance with the regional and economic corridor development plans, which include the Northern Economic Corridor, Northeastern Economic Corridor, Central-Western Economic Corridor, Southern Economic Corridor, Special Border Economic Zones, and Eastern Economic Corridor.",""],[1,"86","1","Regional Supply Chain Connectivity Development","Developing supply chains to connect within and between areas as well as with neighboring areas and other countries.",""],[1,"86","1","Eastern Economic Corridor Upgrading and Technology Transfer","Further developing the Eastern Economic Corridor to ensure balanced and sustainable growth and to become an industrial and service base with advanced technology and innovation by promoting investment and employment in the area as well as encouraging continuous technology transfer.",""],[1,"86","2","Community Economy Strengthening and Local Enterprise Support","Strengthening community economies by using networks in the community, such as households, temples and schools, as key driving mechanisms.",""],[1,"86","3","Local Market Mechanism Management and Supply Chain Innovation","Promoting local management of market mechanisms to forge a balance between local production and consumption and to generate income from external markets.",""],[1,"88","3","Local Enterprise Competitiveness and Supply Chain Linkage Support","Boosting competitiveness of all levels of local enterprises and linking them with the supply chains of external businesses.",""],[1,"88","4","Investment Enabling Measures for Local Trade and Advanced Industries","Forging the private sector's role in developing advanced tech industries by facilitating its business operations through measures on clustering of industries and services.",""],[1,"88","4","Investor and Foreign Expert Incentive Scheme","Offering incentives to attract investors and foreign experts to invest/reside in the development area.",""],[1,"88","4","Investment Finance and Innovation Support","Easing access to funding and innovation in comprehensive business operations and investment with modern technologies.",""],[1,"88","4","Investment Law Review and Revision","Reviewing and revising laws to facilitate investment, especially in the target industry with advanced technology and eco-friendly industries.",""],[1,"88","4","Investor Information and Community Engagement Campaign","Continuously publicizing relevant information to investors along with fostering understanding among local populations to ensure acceptance and support for development.",""]],"26":[[1,"13","1","National Trade, Investment, and Logistics Connectivity Strategy","Implementing strategies to make Thailand the region's key strategic gateway for trade, investment and logistics by enhancing connectivity between areas both domestically and internationally along with developing digital and logistical infrastructure to facilitate trade and investment",""],[1,"60","1","ASEAN Business Partnership and Regional Gateway Strategy","Thailand's future direction should be focused on playing a leading role in forging business partnerships with other ASEAN countries, particularly the Greater Mekong Subregion (GMS) countries with an emphasis on collaboration rather than competition, while making Thailand a strategic gateway and nexus to promote constructive balance in international relations and the economy between the region and the two superpowers so that the region's progress and security are well maintained.",""],[1,"60","1","Thailand-China-Laos Economic Connectivity Strategy","Thailand needs a clear economic development strategy to connect the country, Laos and China together and benefit from transport routes from Nongkhai and Chiangrai provinces into Laos and China, which would stimulate investment in building an agile trilateral economic network and trade system, specifically in Thailand's Northeastern and Northern regions, Laos, and China's southern provinces.",""],[1,"60","2","Supply Chain Integration and Production Base Relocation Attraction","Thailand, therefore, should promptly encourage local businesses in target industries to join the regional and global supply chains by receiving or making investments within international cooperation frameworks to pursue opportunities for economic growth, trade and investment expansion, and the enhancement of Thailand's technological level.",""],[1,"60","2","Eastern Economic Corridor Investment Attraction Strategy","Thailand should also develop proactive strategies to exploit the relocation of production bases in target industries to expand trade and investment with China, the United States, Europe, and Japan based on mutual interests that also meet Thailand's needs by attracting investment from every prospective country to relocate its production base to the Eastern Economic Corridor and other economic zones for linkage to key manufacturing locations in the GMS countries, southern China and Asia at large.",""],[1,"61","3","Negotiation of Additional Economic and Trade Agreements","the country should urgently negotiate more economic, trade and investment agreements with key partners - for example, the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP) as well as agreements with the European Union and the United Kingdom - for optimal benefits in line with the country's needs while retaining the advantages of the local manufacturing and service sectors.",""],[1,"61","3","Trade Agreement Impact Mitigation Fund","A fund should be set up to prevent and mitigate impacts from trade agreements, while economic collaboration should be expanded with countries that can become sources of knowledge in science, technology and innovation in fields required for upgrading Thailand's target industries.",""],[1,"61","3","Expanded International Economic Collaboration for Knowledge Transfer","A fund should be set up to prevent and mitigate impacts from trade agreements, while economic collaboration should be expanded with countries that can become sources of knowledge in science, technology and innovation in fields required for upgrading Thailand's target industries.",""],[1,"61","4","Regulatory Reform for Trade and Logistics Facilitation","Thailand therefore needs to review and revise obstructive regulations, including regulations on cross-border transport, logistics and trade, as well as encouraging local logistics service providers of all scales to embrace digital technologies to facilitate and promote domestic and international trade and investment.",""],[1,"61","5","Integrated Transport Infrastructure Planning","Hence, Thailand should integrate existing development plans for land, water and air transport infrastructure to leverage the country's geographical advantages and infrastructure linkages between the GMS countries and southern China while including the Eastern Economic Corridor and other Special Economic Zones in infrastructure linkages to globalize the local manufacturing and service sectors.",""],[1,"61","6","GMS Transport and Logistics Strategy Formulation","To promote transport and logistics in the GMS, a strategy should be formulated to drive international collaboration and agreements.",""],[1,"61","6","Investment Project Mobilization Team for Transport Linkages","In this context, a team should be set up to mobilize investment projects to expedite transportation linkages with GMS countries and China.",""],[1,"61","6","Supervised Agency for Transport and Logistics Coordination","There should also be an agency under the supervision of the Deputy Prime Minister responsible for high-",""],[1,"62","1","Integrated Trade and Logistics Coordination","coordination among all relevant agencies to ensure integrated, collaborative operations; for example, by having the Ministry of Transport oversee the transports of goods and the Customs Department responsible for Thailand National Single Window system-and a consideration of import tariff reductions for construction materials.","Ministry of Transport | Customs Department"],[1,"62","2","Enabling Trade and Investment Ecosystem Development","These targets are achievable by creating an enabling ecosystem that supports trade and investment for Thailand to become the region's key trade and investment base; enhancing the productivity and opportunities of Thai entrepreneurs to enable linkages to regional and global value chains; and enhancing the competitiveness of Thailand's manufacturing and key service sectors.",""],[1,"62","2","Entrepreneur Productivity and Global Value Chain Linkage Support","These targets are achievable by creating an enabling ecosystem that supports trade and investment for Thailand to become the region's key trade and investment base; enhancing the productivity and opportunities of Thai entrepreneurs to enable linkages to regional and global value chains; and enhancing the competitiveness of Thailand's manufacturing and key service sectors.",""],[1,"62","2","Manufacturing and Key Service Sector Competitiveness Enhancement","These targets are achievable by creating an enabling ecosystem that supports trade and investment for Thailand to become the region's key trade and investment base; enhancing the productivity and opportunities of Thai entrepreneurs to enable linkages to regional and global value chains; and enhancing the competitiveness of Thailand's manufacturing and key service sectors.",""],[1,"62","4","Expanded Bilateral and Multilateral Cooperation","Foreign affairs in expanding bilateral and multilateral collaboration in economy, trade, transport and human resources, especially in the sub-region and in Asia;",""],[1,"62","4","Transport, Logistics, and Digital Systems Upgrade","Infrastructure, logistics and digital systems focusing on enhancing the capability, quality and efficiency of the transport infrastructure and logistics system to increase productivity in the manufacturing and service sectors, reduce production and service costs so as to raise competitiveness in the international market, and promote systematic connections within the region and sub-region;",""],[1,"64","25","Trade and Investment Relationship Development through Free Trade Agreements","Developing trade & investment relationships by pushing for the exploitation of existing free trade agreements & concluding other significant free trade agreements",""],[1,"64","29","Digital Systems for Trade and Investment","Establishing digital systems conducive to trade and investment",""],[1,"65","1","Balanced Bilateral Relations Policy","Maintaining balanced relationships with countries with which Thailand has friendly relations through policies that clearly meet the country's needs.",""],[1,"65","1","Equitable International Cooperation Expansion","Extending collaboration with countries with which Thailand has friendly relations to ensure equitable cooperation.",""],[1,"65","2","National Committee for International Relations Integration","Forging balanced and collective regional development through a national committee to integrate approaches to fostering international relations at all levels.",""],[1,"65","3","Free Trade Agreement Utilization and Negotiation Programme","Developing trade and investment relationships by pushing for the exploitation of existing free trade agreements as well as concluding other significant free trade agreements.",""],[1,"65","3","Trade and Investment Agreement Negotiation Support","Negotiating various agreements supporting trade and investment, such as transport, immigration, and management at border crossing areas.",""],[1,"65","3","Thailand-Laos-China Special Development Zone Collaboration","Building and strengthening collaboration in the special development zones between Thailand, Laos and China to generate economic and social benefits from logistic nexuses at Nongkhai and Chiangrai provinces.",""],[1,"65","4","National Committee for Integrated Investment Promotion Review and Revision","Establishing a mechanism or national committee for integrated approaches to reviewing and revising investment promotion as well as investing in new economic fields to accommodate an ongoing shift of production bases and supply chain realignment across Asia in the form of, for example, tariff and non-tariff privileges.",""],[1,"65","5","Formulation of Laws and Guidelines to Meet International Standards","Formulating laws and guidelines to elevate the country to international standards.",""],[1,"66","8","National Trade Platform Development","Developing a national trade platform to support B2B trade.",""],[1,"66","8","Digitalization of Financial Services for Investment Facilitation","Digitalizing Thailand's financial services to facilitate investments.",""],[1,"66","8","Trade and Investment Legal and Regulatory Reform","Reviewing, revising and developing laws and regulations related to fair trade and trade and investment facilitation.",""]],"27":[[1,"39","28","Tourism Personnel Skills and Capacity Development","Raising tourism personne's skills & capacity in line with businesses needs & sustainable high-quality tourism by focusing on developing competency requirements for each position, boosting entrepreneurs business efficiency and good governance, and developing online learning courses.",""],[1,"39","32","Tourism Destination Management Quality Upgrade","Raising management quality of tourist destinations & related businesses to international standards especially on security, cleanliness, fairness and sustainable environmental management.",""],[1,"39","32","Tourism Enterprise Quality Standards Improvement","Improving basic and advanced quality standards of tourism related enterprises & small businesses with appropriate service levels.",""],[1,"39","32","Tourism Enterprise Accreditation Incentive Scheme","Incentivizing entrepreneurs for accreditation, and pushing for support from public agencies & private sector for accredited enterprises.",""],[1,"39","36","Tourism Sector Employment Registration Facilitation","Encouraging and facilitating personnel in the tourism sector & related services to register on government database& to urism employment registration system by reducing paperwork, boosting convenience, offering incentives.",""],[1,"41","2","Tourism Destination and Business Quality Upgrade Programme","Sub-strategy 3.2 Raising the management quality of tourist destinations and related businesses to international standards especially in relation to security, cleanliness, fairness and sustainable environmental management, such as hygiene measures based on emerging tourism approaches so as to steer towards high-quality tourism as well as \"white tourism\" standards.",""],[1,"41","2","Tourism Enterprise Quality Standards Improvement","Improving basic and advanced quality standards of tourism-related enterprises and small businesses with appropriate service levels.",""],[1,"41","2","Tourism Enterprise Accreditation Incentive Support","Incentivizing entrepreneurs for accreditation, and pushing for support from government agencies and the private sector for accredited enterprises.",""],[1,"41","4","Tourism Personnel Skills and Capacity Development","Supporting tourism personnel's skills and capacity development to achieve quality and sustainability for high-quality tourism such as heartfelt services, understanding and pride in local cultures, language skills, digital communications, storytelling, cleanliness and security, and environmental protection:",""],[1,"41","5","Tourism Personnel Skills and Capacity Development","Sub-strategy 4.1 Enhancing the skills and capacity of tourism personnel in line with the needs of businesses and sustainable high-quality tourism by focusing on developing competency requirements for each job position, boosting entrepreneurs' business efficiency and good governance as well as developing online learning courses to strengthen their knowledge in financial management, marketing, tourism management, and digital technology including effective use of data for improvement.",""],[1,"41","6","Tourism Sector Personnel Registration Facilitation","Encouraging and facilitating personnel in the tourism sector and associated services to register on the government database and tourism employment registration system by easing the procedures, increasing convenience, and offering incentives.",""]],"28":[[1,"57","3","Medical Education Hub Initiative","Promoting the \"medical education hub\" initiative by developing international medical courses as well as trainings for medical personnel in South Asia and ASEAN with internship opportunities, both online and in Thai hospitals, through scholarships from international organizations, third countries or the Thai government.",""],[1,"57","4","International Medical Research and Innovation Collaboration Incentives","Developing incentives and benefits for leading international organizations and foreign experts to take part in the improvement of Thailand's medical research and innovation standards through, for example, research agreements, further expansion of presented works in Thailand, internship/exchange programs at leading institutions, inviting international experts to teach/speak in Thailand, and international presentation of works by Thai researchers.",""],[1,"57","5","Interdisciplinary Research Personnel Development","Developing research personnel with interdisciplinary knowledge and skills in conducting research in science, technology, innovation and digital medicine, and technological innovation and evaluation.",""],[1,"57","5","Research Knowledge Exchange and Skills-Building Network","Facilitating knowledge exchanges and skills building among researchers within the professional community.",""],[1,"57","5","Medical Innovator Incubation Initiative","Continuously incubating medical innovators.",""],[1,"57","5","University Research Engagement Initiative","Encouraging educational institutions to engage in research.",""],[1,"57","5","International Expert Attraction and Health Workforce Retention Mechanism","Attracting more international experts to work in Thailand and transfer knowledge as well as developing mechanisms to retain healthcare personnel, especially by means of appropriate remuneration for research personnel to motivate them to maintain their research profession.",""],[1,"57","6","Research Ecosystem for Commercializing Technological Innovations","Sub-strategy 4.4 Building a research ecosystem to facilitate the commercialization of technological innovations.",""],[1,"57","7","International Research and Development Collaboration Networks","Sub-strategy 4.5 Establishing international networks for collaboration in research and development.",""],[1,"58","1","Medical Technology Transfer Promotion","promote medical technology transfer through, for example, joint research, commissioned research, etc.",""],[1,"58","1","Academic Support and International Training for Medical and Wellness Industry Linkages","Elevating academic support to countries with tendencies to join the value chain network of research and development through scholarships and international training in line with Thailand's development directions for the medical and wellness industry.",""],[1,"58","3","Private Sector Engagement in Medical Workforce Development","Promoting private sector engagement in producing and developing medical personnel with a role in identifying fields with needs, curriculum development, the production as well as upskilling of specialized and interdisciplinary personnel to accommodate high-value medical services, and necessary competency enhancement training.",""],[1,"58","4","Medical Personnel Importation and Shared Staffing Mechanism","Encouraging importation of medical personnel.",""],[1,"58","5","Healthcare Workforce Rotation and Retention Mechanism","Enabling the distribution of healthcare workforce by developing a mechanism to rotate healthcare workforce in terms of geography, workload and areas of shortage.",""],[1,"58","5","Healthcare Worker Incentives and Welfare Improvement Package","Offering incentives to healthcare workers to remain in the public health system, such as career paths, job promotions and capacity development opportunities for personnel in remote areas, reductions of workload, and improvement of basic welfare system to ensure good quality of life.",""]],"29":[[1,"12","3","Electric Vehicle Industry Transformation","3) Transforming the automobile industry into an electric vehicle industry throughout the supply chain with the support of investments in research and development in order to boost the capacity of Thai manufacturers while preparing the",""],[1,"43","2","Next-Generation Automotive and EV Support Measures","The Thai government has promoted the next-generation automotive industry by emphasizing an expansion of the current industry onto more advanced technology and innovation together with determining key supportive measures for EVs, such as foreign and domestic market stimulation measures, supportive measures for demand stimulation and transition towards EV manufacturing, and systematic infrastructure preparedness measures.",""],[1,"43","3","Comprehensive Electric Vehicle System Development","the Thai government has expedited the development of a comprehensive EV system",""],[1,"43","4","Electric Vehicle Industry Development Acceleration","Based on the context and Thailand's automotive industry development policies, goals have been formulated for the next phase of Thailand's EV industry development acceleration in three areas with an aim to achieve the targets set by the National Electric Vehicle Policy Committee and to effectively mitigate environmental impacts.",""],[1,"43","4","Domestic and Export EV Demand Expansion","1) To increase domestic consumption and export demand for all types of EVs by establishing consumption demand for the domestic market and export demand for EVs, especially hybrids and plug-in hybrids which play a significant role in familiarizing consumers over the transitional period;",""],[1,"43","4","EV Production Conversion and Technology Investment Support","2) To encourage existing operators to shift to EV production, and to support key technology investment in",""],[1,"44","1","Domestic Electric Vehicle Production and Ecosystem Development","domestic EV production in order to enable the industry to meet global trends and emerging needs, to facilitate manufacturers of vehicle parts in shifting to EV industry or other appropriate businesses, and to mitigate the impacts affecting internal combustion vehicle manufacturers and other affected businesses; and 3) To build an ecosystem of supporting factors focusing on human resources development, investment in large-scale battery factories and development of relevant standards.",""],[1,"44","2","Electric Vehicle Industry Transition Support","Milestone 3 is set to cover a five-year transitional period with a focus on fully supporting the EV industry to become a new leading industry and helping the country to emerge as a production base of EVs by manufacturing main parts simultaneously with shifting the production base of internal combustion vehicles towards EVs without abandoning high-potential export markets so as to maintain balance and the production capacity at more than 2 million units per year during the transition period, as well as supporting different tiers of manufacturers of conventional automotive parts to transition and become manufacturers in the EV industry.",""],[1,"44","4","Smart Automotive Industry Transition","transitioning the entire automotive industry into a smart automotive industry, supporting technology and the development of energy storage system, promoting investment in research and development and technology transfers, as well as encouraging the local automotive industry to achieve international standards.",""],[1,"46","6","Electric Vehicle Production Transition and Technology Investment Support","To ensure that existing businesses can transition into EV production and there are investments in key EV technology in the country",""],[1,"46","14","Electric Vehicle Supply Chain Business Expansion","Businesses In EV supply chain Increase by no less than 14/ rwvestments In kay EV technology occur by 2027",""],[1,"46","33","Electric Vehicle Incentive Measures","Promoting incentive measures to boost shift to EV's",""],[1,"46","45","Low-Interest Rate Loan Provision","Providing Low- interest rate loans",""],[1,"47","1","Electric Vehicle Incentive Package","Promoting incentives to encourage a shift to EVs, including 1) tax incentives such as an excise tax, waiver or reduction of annual vehicle registration fees, etc., 2) non-tax incentives such as discounts on household and condominium electricity bills, free parking, and hire-purchase loans for EV users, and 3) subsidies for EV purchases to lower operational costs to similar level as those of internal combustion vehicles.",""],[1,"47","2","Conditional Procurement Mechanism for Electric Vehicle Adoption","Promoting the use of all types of EVs in public transport systems, government agencies, state enterprises and public organizations through a conditional procurement mechanism to promote domestic production and human resources development in the EV industry.",""],[1,"47","3","Internal Combustion Vehicle Conversion to Modified EVs","Encouraging people to convert existing internal combustion vehicles into modified EVs with safety standards certification and registration.",""],[1,"47","5","EV Export Market Expansion Strategy","Fostering EV export market expansion while retaining existing export bases in Thailand's main trade partners for competitive products, particularly pickup trucks.",""],[1,"47","6","BEV Export Promotion Strategy","Promoting BEV exports, especially to countries with carbon- neutral policies to encourage the use of such vehicles.",""],[1,"47","7","Automotive Industry Transition to Electric Vehicles","Formulating goals and plans for a systematic, concrete transition of the existing automotive industry throughout the supply chain to the EV industry within five years:",""],[1,"47","8","EV Production Base and Supply Chain Capability Support","Promoting Thailand as a key EV production base to attract foreign investment in ZEV manufacturing, as well as supporting businesses within the supply chain to become capable of manufacturing key parts in EV technology, including connected and autonomous vehicles.",""],[1,"47","9","Clean, Economical and Safe Vehicle Production Promotion","Encouraging the production of \"clean, economical and safe\" vehicles according to international standards (UN regulations) to improve the quality of vehicles for domestic use and meet the diverse needs of current and new export markets.",""],[1,"47","10","Domestic Battery and Key Parts Production Base Development","Enabling the establishment of a domestic production base for batteries and key parts such as motors, battery management systems and navigation systems.",""],[1,"47","11","Supply Chain Connectivity for ZEV Raw Materials","Fostering supply chain connections with countries with important raw materials for ZEV production, including rare earth minerals and semiconductors.",""],[1,"47","12","Electrification of National Product Champions","Expediting a shift towards electrification of national product champions such as pickup trucks, eco-cars and motorcycles.",""],[1,"48","2","EV Production Line Conversion Support","Encouraging existing operators with potentials to shift to EV production lines such as production with new materials of auto bodies and suspension systems, the production of power transmission systems, etc.",""],[1,"48","5","Support for Automotive Transition Technologies","Promoting progressive development to facilitate businesses' transition and minimize economic impacts during the transitional period by supporting automotive technologies with potentials such as hybrids, plug-in hybrids, etc. in order to build momentum to become manufacturers in the BEV supply chain.",""],[1,"48","5","ICT Adoption for Manufacturing Efficiency","Encouraging domestic manufacturers to use ICT to increase production management efficiency.",""],[1,"48","6","Financial and Tax Incentives for Investment","Providing benefits to boost investment by means of financial and tax measures.",""],[1,"48","6","Partnerships with Leading EV Countries","Forging partnerships with leading EV countries to seek appropriate measures to assist in the transition of Thai enterprises and boost competitiveness of Thai start-ups on the international market.",""],[1,"48","7","Technology Adoption in Production Management","Advocating for the adoption of technologies such as autonomous systems, artificial intelligence, other 4.0 industries, as well as 5G wireless mobile technology in production management to cut costs and raise competitiveness.",""],[1,"48","8","Conversion of Existing Internal Combustion Cars to Electric Vehicles","Promoting the conversion of existing internal combustions cars into EVs to stimulate investment in the automotive industry's ecosystem and the transfer of EV technology.",""],[1,"48","9","EV Joint Venture and Business Partnership Promotion","Promoting joint ventures/business partnerships between Thai businesses in the existing supply chain and foreign manufacturers of EVs or parts to promote technology and resource transfer as well as to enhance Thai enterprises' development opportunities to become product and technology owners.",""],[1,"48","10","Enterprise Transition Support for Internal Combustion Engine and Power Transmission Firms","Supporting enterprises in internal combustion engines and power transmission systems in their transition to other industries such as industrial robotics, rail or other industries with potentials.",""],[1,"48","11","Remedy Measures for Workers and Farmers Affected by EV Industry Transition","Sub-strategy 5.2 Establishing remedy measures for those affected by the shift to an EV industry such as operators and workers in the petrochemical businesses and farmers of biofuel crops.",""],[1,"49","1","Electric Vehicle System Development","system for EVs.",""],[1,"49","11","EV Industry Human Resource Development and Transition Support","Developing human resources to support the EV industry and providing remedies during transition, as well as promoting lifelong learning.",""],[1,"49","12","Business-Education Collaboration for EV Technology Knowledge Transfer","Promoting collaboration between businesses and educational institutions to boost knowledge transfer of the EV technology, particularly in relation to battery technology, sensor system and EV electronics system.",""],[1,"50","1","Incentives to Attract High-Skilled Thai and Foreign Experts","Setting measures to attract highly skilled Thai and foreign experts with benefits offered at the preliminary periods, such as tax benefits for high-skilled workforce in fields related to EV production, privileges in visa, residency and migration for foreign experts.",""],[1,"50","9","Financial Support for Clean-Energy Automotive Investment","Providing financial supports to businesses investing in the clean-energy automotive industry:",""],[1,"50","10","Low-Interest Loan Support for EV and Parts Businesses","Providing low-interest rate loans to EV-and-parts businesses.",""]],"30":[[1,"43","2","Nationwide EV Charging Infrastructure Development","In addition, the government has also supported the development of nationwide infrastructure, particularly charging stations.",""],[1,"46","39","EV Charging Station Investment and Development Support","Supporting investment & development of EV charging stations to fit cormier behavion",""],[1,"46","55","Electrical Grid Reinforcement for EV Charging","Supporting electrical grids reinforcement to sufficiently meet charging dernand & separating electricity bill for EV charging from other electricity -",""],[1,"49","2","EV Research and Development Infrastructure Support","Encouraging manufacturers of EVs and parts to use the government-built intellectual infrastructure for research and development, such as the National Automatic and Tire Testing, the Research and Innovation Center, and a battery-testing laboratory in Sanam Chai Khet District, Chachoengsao Province.",""],[1,"49","4","EV Charging Station Investment and Development Support","Supporting the investment and development of EV charging stations or chargers to fit consumer behaviors and daily routines at home, office, places of accommodation and public spaces.",""],[1,"49","5","Electric Grid Reinforcement for EV Charging Demand","Supporting the reinforcement of electrical grids to sufficiently meet the constant charging demand of increasing EV use, together with separating electricity bills for EV charging from other electricity usage.",""],[1,"49","6","Smart Grid and EV Charging Integration Platform","Promoting the smart grid technology to fully integrate the connections and management of EV charging, including the development of smart meters as well as an integrated platform to link data from charging stations and EVs for the purpose of grid management.",""],[1,"50","11","EV Infrastructure Investment Fund","Encouraging the establishment of a fund for investment in EV infrastructure and management related to the green and circular economies.",""]],"31":[[1,"46","40","EV Industry and Charging Station Regulatory Reform","Revising & crafting regulations to facilitate development of EV inchastry & charging stations",""],[1,"46","54","Regulatory Framework for Emerging Vehicle and Electrification Technologies","Promoting nowarch and formulating regulations to 2:000mmodate R&Din ZEVI, autonomous wwhicles, electrical. connectors, electrification and shareci ut",""],[1,"46","67","Promotion of Investment in Domestic Test Centers","58.6 Promoting investment in domedic test centers",""],[1,"49","3","ZEV and Autonomous Vehicle R&D Support Regulations","Promoting researches and formulating regulations to support research and development in ZEVs and autonomous vehicles as well as electrical connectors, electrification and shared use in order to extend results in the domestic industrial sector afterward.",""],[1,"49","7","EV Industry and Charging Station Regulatory Reform","Drafting and amending laws and regulations to facilitate the growth of the EV industry and charging stations together with regulations on communications and safety, installation and area development, and used batteries.",""],[1,"49","8","Relaxation of Regulations for EV Parts Supply Chain Investment","Relaxing regulations related to investment in supply chains of EVs parts that will be vital at the initial stage to boost foreign direct investments.",""],[1,"49","9","Vehicle Registration Regulation Revision for EV Conversion","Reviewing and revising relevant regulations (particularly in relation to vehicle registration) to encourage and facilitate conversion to EVs.",""],[1,"50","2","EV Standards Development and Accreditation Enhancement","Establishing and developing standards for EVs, parts and accessories in line with export markets' standards and requirements.",""],[1,"50","3","EV Standards Promotion and Conversion Support","Identifying key standards to promote conversion to EVs and the manufacturing of battery, charging stations and other EV accessories.",""],[1,"50","4","Standard Development Plans for EV Businesses","Sub-strategy 10.3 Formulating standard development plans for EV businesses.",""],[1,"50","5","National Automotive and Tire Test Center Capacity Enhancement for EV Testing","Developing and enhancing the capacity of the National Automotive and Tire Test Center in testing EVs and parts in full compliance with international standards and requirements.",""],[1,"50","6","Standards and Certification Agency for Converted Vehicles","Identifying standards and designated agency responsible for certifying converted vehicles.",""],[1,"50","7","Domestic Test Center Investment for Industrial and EV Standards","Encouraging investment in domestic test centers to achieve industrial standards and standards for EV manufacturers, product liabilities, and quality management through collaboration with international accreditation organizations.",""],[1,"50","8","Converted Vehicle Standards and EV Conversion Regulation Reform","Developing key standards - namely, installation standards and battery standards for converted vehicles - to build confidence in the safety of converted vehicles.",""]],"32":[[1,"71","14","Attract Major Technology Company Investment","At least three af the world's biggest tech companies invest in Thailand by 2027",""],[1,"71","17","International Internet Traffic Exchange Point Development","Thailand has internacional internet traffic connecting & exchange pointla) to boost capital servicon competidwerwm by 2027",""],[1,"72","3","Digital Platforms for Infrastructure and Government Services","Encouraging the use of technology in infrastructure management and government services by designing digital platforms to support all dimensions of development, such as platforms for energy trade, carbon market, smart city, telemedicine and online education.",""],[1,"73","4","Attract Big Tech Investment in Digital Infrastructure","Attracting big tech investment in Thailand's digital infrastructure, (e.g. data centers, e-government, cloud, and virtual platforms).",""],[1,"73","5","Digital Infrastructure Development for Competitiveness","Supporting the development of digital infrastructure to help Thailand leverage its geographical advantages to enhance the competitiveness of Thailand's digital services by 2027 by, for example, expanding international internet bandwidth, linking international networks to cut costs and times for building data centers, and developing domestic public cloud services.",""],[1,"73","6","Pilot User-Friendly Digital Solutions for Local and ASEAN Markets","Developing and elevating the competitiveness of manufacturers, developers, designers, and system builders in the local digital industry and services to become providers of user-friendly digital solutions that meet the needs of local or ASEAN markets by piloting in the fields of agriculture, medicine and wellness, tourism, and local administrative management.",""]],"33":[[1,"75","4","SME Promotion and Development System Reform","the public sector needs to promptly improve and enhance the efficiency of the SME promotion and development system to become more relevant to the needs of entrepreneurs and based on an understanding of diverse businesses, as well as incentivizing SMEs to join the system and undertake development in an inclusive and equal manner",""],[1,"78","27","Regulatory Revision to Remove Business Obstacles","Expediting a revision of regulations obstructing business operations to ensure equitable competition betwoon SMEs and large businesses",""],[1,"79","1","Regulatory Reform for Fair Business Competition","Expediting a revision of regulations obstructing business operations to ensure equitable competition between SMEs and large businesses by developing competitive behavior monitoring tools to be used in formulating corrective and control measures against market domination.",""],[1,"79","1","Business Operation Guidelines Enforcement","Articulating, and strictly enforcing, business operation guidelines to ensure appropriate and equitable competition among entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"79","2","SME Business Registration and Approval Simplification","reducing steps and timeframes in new business registrations and approvals",""],[1,"79","2","E-Government Platform for Public Services","Developing an e- government platform for all procedures regarding public services",""],[1,"79","2","Business Support Center Strengthening","Raising the efficiency of the Business Support Centers to assist entrepreneurs in starting and conducting businesses",""],[1,"79","2","Business Operation Manual Development and Dissemination","developing and disseminating business operation manuals that include every business category and are accessible to entrepreneurs",""],[1,"79","4","One ID System for SMEs","Sub-Strategy 2.1 Establishing one ID system for SMEs and encouraging SMEs to adopt the system in digital transactions.",""],[1,"79","4","Simplification of Government Transaction Procedures","Reducing steps and paperwork required in government transactions.",""]],"34":[[1,"78","22","SME Financing Mechanisms Development","Strategy 3 Building financial. mechanisms compatible with unique characteristics of SMEs to ensure all SVE groups have a comprehensive access to funding",""],[1,"78","29","Alternative Credit Assessment for SME Lending","Encouraging financial. institutions, banks, and non-financial institutions to use business data and digital footprints in approving loans to SME>",""],[1,"78","33","Specialized Financial Institutions SME Loan and Guarantee Measures","Determining the role of Specialized Financial. Institutiona (SAs) to include clear measures on loans and guarantees for each SME segment, particularly for small and micro enterprises",""],[1,"79","7","Digital Credit Assessment for SME Lending","Encouraging financial institutions, banks, and non-financial institutions to use business data and digital footprints in approving loans to SMEs by using digital",""],[1,"80","2","Special Loan Schemes for SME Segments","Sub-strategy 3.2 Determining the role of Specialized Financial Institutions (SFIs) to include clear measures on loans and guarantees for each SME segment, particularly for small and micro enterprises.",""],[1,"80","3","SME Alternative Financing Expansion","Sub-strategy 3.3 Encouraging SMEs to raise funds through capital markets or diverse sources in line with their business models in addition to conventional loans.",""]],"35":[[1,"78","25","Startup and Innovation-Driven Entrepreneurship Support","Creating enabling ecosystem conducive for startups & Innovation- driven entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"78","25","Startup Financing and International Market Linkage Support","Providing access to appropriane funding sources and linkages to International networks & markets",""],[1,"78","36","Business Regulatory Reform for Startups and Company Formation","Reviewing and revising laws to increase ease of business operationa, especially those for startups wag. wwcruiting globally-acknowledged technological, expertise & company formation specialists",""],[1,"78","37","Organic Law Enactment under the Social Enterprise Promotion Act","Enacting organic law under the Social. Enterprise Promotion Act A.E. 2562(2019)",""],[1,"78","47","Startup International Market Linkage and Incubation Participation Support","Supporting a linkage between startupn and the international market & promoting participation in incutution programs especially international incubation",""],[1,"81","3","Startup Business Regulatory Reform","Sub-strategy 6.1 Reviewing and revising laws to increase ease of business operations, especially those for startups.",""],[1,"81","3","Startup Ecosystem Capacity Recruitment","For example, recruiting personnel with globally acknowledged technological expertise and company formation specialists to develop an enabling ecosystem as well as advance startups who require an ecosystem and business practices in starting, running, and progressing unconventional businesses.",""],[1,"81","4","Public-Private Partnership Seed Funding and Private Equity Support","Alleviating constraints on fundraising to allow public-private partnerships in developing seed funding and private equity funds for individuals, which give startups mentors in business building.",""],[1,"81","5","Startup International Market Linkage and Incubation Support","Supporting a linkage between startups and the international market by encouraging startups to participate in incubation programs, especially international incubation.",""],[1,"81","5","Startup Collaboration with Special Development Zones and Foreign Universities","Fostering collaboration with special development zones for startups and leading foreign universities in order to give young startups opportunities to achieve Series C or higher status.",""],[1,"81","6","Organic Law for Social Enterprise Registration Facilitation","Enacting an organic law under the Social Enterprise Promotion Act B.E. 2562 (2019) to mitigate constraints in social enterprise registrations to encourage more registrations by non-juristic enterprises.",""],[1,"81","6","Social Enterprise Fund Establishment","Stimulating the setting up of social enterprise funds.",""],[1,"81","7","Sustainable Business Model Development for Social Enterprises","Supporting the development of specific sustainable business models for social enterprises through collaborative mechanisms among the public sector, the private sector and the Social Enterprise Association.",""],[1,"81","8","Joint Investment Incentives for Social Enterprises","Offering benefits and incentives for joint investment with social enterprises to encourage large private companies to correspond with corporate social responsibility policies by supporting the growth of domestic social enterprises.",""]],"36":[[1,"80","6","International Trade Platform Support for SMEs","Developing international trade platforms accessible to SMEs and allowing domestic SMEs to leverage safe and secure country's platforms in order to facilitate access to potential markets in other countries.",""],[1,"80","6","SME Export Capability and Trade Privilege Support","Stimulating SMEs with export capabilities to use trade privileges.",""],[1,"80","6","FTA Adjustment Preparedness and Remedies","providing preparedness and remedies for people who are affected by Free Trade Agreements (FTA) and international collaborative frameworks.",""]],"37":[[1,"87","1","Universal Design Urban Infrastructure and Housing Security Initiative","Increasing access to urban infrastructure, such as urban design based on the universal design principles and housing security.",""],[1,"87","1","Inclusive Welfare Support for Urban Vulnerable Groups","Providing inclusive welfare for all inhabitants in order to improve quality of life for vulnerable groups to ensure good physical and mental health.",""],[1,"87","1","Urban Community Network Capacity-Building for Vulnerable Groups","Increasing the capacity of urban community networks to assist and provide initial care for the vulnerable both in normal time and during crises.",""],[1,"87","2","Urban Development Charters and Urban Development Companies","Promoting urban development through various forms, including urban development charters and urban development companies.",""],[1,"87","2","Strengthening Urban Development Charter Mechanisms","Exploring the feasibility of enhancing the charters' driving mechanisms to ensure continuity in urban development.",""],[1,"87","2","Urban Development Scaling Based on the Khon Kaen Model","Taking lessons from successful cases such as the Khon Kaen model, which attracts investment and boost the employment of locals, to scale up in other areas.",""],[1,"87","2","Social Enterprise Support for Urban Development","Promoting the role of social enterprises in area and urban development, as well as in developing new businesses and creating jobs, by providing initial protection measures from business and financial risks.",""],[1,"87","2","Community Skills and Urban Farming for Self-Reliance","Imparting skills and knowledge to the community for self-reliance; for example, through health enterprises for social benefits, which focus on urban farming as well as making the city a food safety zone.",""],[1,"87","2","Urban Social Enterprise Network Expansion","Expanding the network to connect together social enterprises in the development area and city to foster sustainable economic and social security.",""],[1,"87","2","Regulatory Reform for Government-Partner Collaboration","Revising government regulations to better allow collaboration between the government and development partners, including the private sector, the public, and civil society.",""],[1,"87","2","Collective Urban Planning and Implementation","Promoting collective planning and implementation to ensure the appropriateness, flexibility and agility of solutions.",""],[1,"87","5","Urban Land Readjustment and Participatory Planning","Encouraging land readjustment process together with the development plan of the adjusted lands with public participation following the livable and",""],[1,"88","1","Sustainable City Framework","sustainable city framework.",""],[1,"88","1","Urban Landscape Improvement","Improving the landscape in line with urban culture and environment.",""],[1,"88","1","Urban Green and Public Space Expansion","Increasing green and public areas in the city as well as diminishing urban sprawls to improve residents' quality of life.",""],[1,"89","1","Cross-Sector Urban Investment Planning","Pushing for key development areas and cities to develop investment plans in line with the development plan based on cross-sectoral participation, such as livable and sustainable cities and urban development charters, to ensure concrete implementation.",""],[1,"89","1","City Economic Revival Investment Plan","These include an investment plan to revive a city's economy in specific development area or high value economic zones and plan to invest in, and develop, a mass transit system to connect and provide convenience to all groups of the population.",""],[1,"89","2","Tax Support for Social Enterprise and Public-Benefit Urban Development","Improving tax measures to support social enterprise activities on urban development and land use for public benefit, such as urban agriculture.",""],[1,"89","2","Local Development and Health Improvement Fund","Exploring the possibility of setting up funds for new initiatives, such as a fund for structural and environmental improvements for health benefits that prioritize the design and restoration of buildings and the environment for economic activities, housing, and disease prevention and control.",""],[1,"89","2","Cultural Preservation Incentive Mechanisms","Designing and experimenting with diverse incentive mechanisms for cultural preservation of key development areas and cities, including historical towns and historic building clusters, as well as the surrounding or co-existing communities.",""]],"38":[[1,"88","1","Transit-Oriented Development Feasibility Study","Supporting a feasibility study on land and structural use to accommodate the Transit Oriented Development.",""],[1,"88","5","Local and Urban Planning Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of local actors at all levels to ensure effective development area and urban management.",""],[1,"88","5","Sustainable City and Area Planning Support","Supporting development area and city planning to ensure sustainability and livability according to the boundaries of ecological spatial plans.",""],[1,"88","5","Urban Sustainability Data and Indicator Framework","Applying data and indicators in assessing a city's sustainability while formulating development strategies with participation of all local partners during every step.",""],[1,"89","1","Local Government Capacity and Urban Management Research","Promoting research and study on the tools and power of local governments in development areas along with urban management to ascertain their ability to cope with the challenges of the VUCA (volatility, uncertainty, complexity and ambiguity) of the world.",""],[1,"89","3","Area and Urban Development Monitoring and Evaluation System","Establishing a monitoring and evaluation system for area and urban development with a focus on a learning process to improve and develop creative innovations for local development.",""],[1,"89","3","Evaluation Funding for Area and Urban Development Projects","Funding the evaluation of area and urban development with a focus on targets, outcomes, and impacts, particularly for important projects in terms of budget size and spatial coverage.",""],[1,"89","3","Public Participation in Local Development Evaluation","Encouraging public participation and awareness in the evaluation of area and urban development by allowing the public to make suggestions to ensure the accountability of local governments.",""]],"39":[[1,"93","23","Intergenerational Poor Household Support and Capacity-Building Programme","Providing aid & building capacity of intergenerational poor household e.g. giving job opportunities with higher productivity & income, building financial skills, providing mentors to advise, inspire and assist throughout the process",""],[1,"94","1","Intergenerational Poor Household Support and Capacity-Building Programme","Providing aid and building the capacity of intergenerational poor households to ensure suitable living conditions for child development.",""],[1,"94","1","Labor Skills Development and Productive Job Placement Support","Putting an emphasis on building job opportunities with higher productivity and income through labor skill development.",""],[1,"94","1","Livelihood Finance, Financial Literacy, and Mentorship Support","Supporting access to finance and necessary resources to make a living, enhancing financial knowledge and skills, together with providing mentors to advise, inspire and assist throughout the process.",""]],"40":[[1,"90","3","Education and Skills Development for Intergenerationally Poor Children","Therefore, the eradication of intergenerational poverty by providing intergenerationally poor children with education and skills development to allow them to reach their full potentials as well as sustainably lifting their families out of poverty is critical to the country's development during the implementation of the 13th National Economic and Social Development Plan.",""],[1,"93","24","Child Support Grant System for Early Childhood Care","Supporting intergenerational poor households in providing quality care to children from gestation to early childhood through child support grant system to support effective child-raising",""],[1,"93","25","Education and Vocational Training Support for Poor Households","Boosting opportunities for quality education and professional skills development by subsidizing & providing necessary resources to children from intergenerational. poor households to return to school, or vocation training",""],[1,"94","3","Child Support Grant System Reform","Increasing the efficiency of Child Support Grant system by addressing exclusion errors, adopting conditional disbursement processes that triggers desired outcomes, and revising eligibility criteria and benefits to align with economic and social conditions.",""],[1,"94","4","Educational Subsidies and Support for Children from Intergenerational Poor Households","Subsidizing and providing necessary resources to children from intergenerational poor households to ease the burden of educational expenses in and outside schools and in both physical and virtual classrooms.",""],[1,"94","4","Monitoring and Support System for Returning Poor Children to Education or Skills Development","Developing a monitoring and support system to help poor children return to education or professional skills development as appropriate.",""],[1,"119","1","Support for Gifted Learners","Providing special support for gifted learners by developing a system to identify, manage and support gifted learners according to the Multiple Intelligences theory by means of scholarships, internships in leading organizations and professional jobs where they can utilize their gifts to their fullest potentials;",""],[1,"119","1","Special Needs Learner Support and Inclusion Mechanisms","providing learners with special needs with diverse opportunities and access to education, including education options for dropout students.",""],[1,"122","2","Inclusive Learning Materials Development","Creating learning materials that leave no one behind by designing learning materials in local dialects and languages for linguistic minorities.",""],[1,"122","2","Accessible Learning Materials for Learners with Disabilities","Producing alternative learning materials for learners with sight and hearing disabilities.",""],[1,"122","2","Affordable Learning Materials Support","Enabling learners with economic constraints to have access to affordable learning materials.",""],[1,"122","5","Capacity Building for Education Personnel on Special Learner Support","Equipping all levels of relevant personnel in the education sector with understanding and capacity to develop learners in special target groups who have complex needs.",""]],"41":[[1,"93","26","Early Childhood Development Center Expansion and Quality Improvement","Increasing access to / urgently improving quality of early childhood development centers nationwide.",""],[1,"93","26","Quality Nursery Access for Children Aged 0-2","Increasing access to quality nurseries for children aged 0-2.",""],[1,"94","5","Expansion and Quality Improvement of Early Childhood Development Centers","Increasing access to and urgently improve the quality and standard of early childhood development centers (child development centers) nationwide.",""],[1,"94","5","Expansion of Child Care Centers for Children Aged 0 to 2","Increasing access to quality child care centers for children aged 0 to two years old, together with supporting local administrative organizations with readiness to expand the services of early childhood development centers to include children aged 0 to two.",""],[1,"94","5","Community, Workplace, and Government Child Care Center Establishment","Promoting the establishment of quality child care centers in communities, workplaces and government agencies in order to allow parents to return to the labor market while living with their children.",""],[1,"118","2","Parent and Guardian Preparedness and Early Childhood Service Coordination","Building preparedness for parents/guardians as well as collaborative mechanisms to provide pregnant women with quality services and provide children with age- appropriate development from conception to the age of six;",""],[1,"118","3","Teacher and Caregiver Early Childhood Development Training","Equipping teachers and caregivers with adequate knowledge and child-caring skills, especially with early childhood development psychology and the ability to work with parents /guardians in promoting child learning and age-appropriate development in line with brain development, physical development, and healthcare and nutrition to stimulate good and balanced development in children before school age;",""],[1,"118","4","Early Childhood Development Facility Upgrading and Resource Support","Raising the standards of early childhood development facilities and providing sufficient resources to become a quality mechanism for early childhood development at the local level;",""],[1,"118","5","Early Childhood Learning and Protection Environment Development","Creating an environment conducive to the learning and protection of children in early childhood to ensure their balanced development and age-appropriate cognitive abilities.",""],[1,"118","5","Multi-Stakeholder Early Childhood Participation Mechanism","Encouraging participation of family, community, local administrative organizations, civil society and the private sector in the process.",""],[1,"118","5","Child Information System for Educational Continuity","Developing informational systems with individual records for each child to pass on to educational institutions to ensure continuous development.",""]],"42":[[1,"93","27","Social Protection Expansion for Working-Age Population","Enhancing social protection to ensure security for working age population",""],[1,"93","27","Social Security System Upgrade for Informal Workers","Uplifting social security System to respond to informal sector workers\" needs to attract them to join System.",""],[1,"93","27","Retirement Savings Promotion","Encouraging retirement savings.",""],[1,"93","27","Labor Welfare Protection Reform for New Forms of Employment","Revising labor welfare protection System to include new forms of employments",""],[1,"94","6","Social Security System Reform for Informal Workers","Uplifting the social security system to respond to the needs of informal workers, specifically improving procedures for contribution payments and benefits to increase variety and flexibility.",""],[1,"94","6","Voluntary Retirement Savings Incentive Scheme","Encouraging retirement savings by incentivizing informal workers to join the voluntary saving system.",""],[1,"94","6","Retirement Savings System Revision","Revising the conditions and benefits of the retirement saving system to allow participants to save and receive increased benefits.",""],[1,"95","1","Labor Welfare Protection System Reform","Revising and developing laws to enhance the labor welfare protection system by including new forms of employments, such as temporary workers and platform workers, and ensuring equal or similar protection as traditional employees.",""]],"43":[[1,"93","28","Alternative Welfare Systems for the Elderly","Improving quality of life for the elderly through altemative welfare systems provided by PAD and other development partners.",""],[1,"95","2","Alternative Elderly Welfare Support Systems","Particularly supporting alternative welfare systems provided by local administrative organizations and other development partners.",""],[1,"95","2","Integrated Elderly Welfare and Financial Support Data System","Integrating data on welfare and financial support for the elderly to avoid duplication and facilitate the provision of targeted assistance to the elderly poor.",""],[1,"95","2","Long-Term Healthcare Access for Dependent Elderly","Improving access to long-term healthcare for the dependent elderly by enhancing the capacity of the Universal Health Coverage program.",""],[1,"95","2","Community-Based Elderly Care Support","Promoting the role of local administrative organizations, private facilities, independent caregivers and trained/qualified family members.",""],[1,"95","2","Elderly Home Living and Housing Improvement","Encouraging the elderly to reside in their homes by improving living conditions, especially for the elderly poor, as well as ensuring adequate housing options, including housings for those who need special care and housings specially designed for the elderly.",""],[1,"120","7","Older Persons Social Participation and Lifelong Learning Programme","Encouraging the elderly to become drivers of social change.",""],[1,"120","8","Elderly Lifestyle Support Environment Development","Creating a supporting environment to correspond to the elderly's lifestyles so as to ensure a happy life and wellbeing.",""],[1,"120","8","Intergenerational Awareness on Ageing","Fostering an understanding of old age among people of other age groups.",""],[1,"120","8","Innovation Support for Elderly Lifestyles","Developing innovations to support the elderly's lifestyles.",""]],"44":[[1,"90","4","Social Protection System Development","Thailand needs to develop adequate social protection systems for populations across different age groups in order to cope effectively with demographic and other changes.",""],[1,"93","30","Integrated Individual Database Development and Updating","Developing& updating individuals\" database covering avery population in intergenerational. poor households.",""],[1,"93","31","Local Mechanisms to Address Intergenerational Poverty","Developing local-level mechanisms to address intergenerational transmission of poverty with a focus on enhancing capacity & role of regional and local agencies and using databases to resolve intergenerational poverty sustainably",""],[1,"94","2","Local-Level Mechanisms to Address Intergenerational Poverty","Sub-strategy 1.2 Developing local-level mechanisms to address intergenerational transmission of poverty with a focus on enhancing the capacity and increasing the role of regional and local agencies in addressing intergenerational poverty.",""],[1,"94","2","Cross-Sectoral Coordination for Intergenerational Poverty Reduction","Integrating cross-sectoral collaboration to drive development strategies while using databases to identify intergenerational poor households, examine their needs, create operational guidelines to resolve their problems, and ensure close monitoring and evaluation in order to resolve intergenerational transmission of poverty sustainably.",""],[1,"95","3","Integrated Social Protection System Reform","Sub-strategy 4.1 Integrating the social protection system starting from collaboratively setting goals of social security provision, establishing clear structures and roles of relevant agencies at the national, regional and local levels and linking databases of all agencies to enable collaboration so as to reduce duplications between projects and measures.",""],[1,"95","3","Benefit Adequacy Improvement for Social Protection","Improving the adequacy of benefits.",""],[1,"95","3","Social Protection Inclusion for Vulnerable Groups","Reducing exclusion errors of vulnerable groups; namely, people with disabilities, homeless people, people with multiple vulnerabilities and people facing difficulties.",""],[1,"95","7","Intergenerational Poverty Database Development and Updating","Developing and updating individuals' database that covers population from intergenerational poor households.",""],[1,"95","8","Database Use for Policy Design and Monitoring","Promoting the utilization of databases in designing policies and measures as well as in monitoring and evaluation to help provide the targeted intergenerational",""]],"45":[[1,"95","4","Social Protection Efficiency and Fiscal Sustainability Reform","Focusing on a careful evaluation of every project/measure to improve efficiency and effectiveness of social protection programs.",""],[1,"95","4","Budget Rationalization for Low-Impact Social Protection Measures","Terminating or reducing budgets of projects/measures with no or low impacts to truly align budgeting with the country's development goals.",""],[1,"95","4","Co-payment Based Social Protection Financing","Promoting social protection financed by co-payments, especially for groups with capacities.",""],[1,"95","4","Local Government Welfare Delivery Support","Supporting the role of local administrative organizations in providing welfare to local populations.",""],[1,"95","4","Tax System Participation Expansion","Attracting more participation in the tax systems.",""],[1,"95","5","Emergency Preparedness and Response System","Identifying levels, approaches and channels for monetary and non-monetary relief, as well as preparing database of target groups, initial budget sources, and the role of relevant national, regional and local agencies in providing support to those affected by socio-economic crises and natural disaster to ensure timely and effective assistance.",""]],"46":[[1,"3","4","Bio-Circular-Green Economy Model","Bio-Circular-Green Economy Model (BCG Model) by focusing on scientific, technological and innovative knowledge to create added economic value and strive for a balance between the conservation and use of the natural resources base and biodiversity.",""],[1,"3","4","Transformation of Manufacturing, Services, and Consumption Formats","The model also aims to transform manufacturing, services and consumption formats in order to reduce impacts on the environment.",""],[1,"17","4","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Measures","Thailand has announced its goal to reduce its greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions and implement measures regarding climate change after 2020",""],[1,"17","4","Forest and Land Use Carbon Absorption Enhancement","plans to enhance the CO2 absorption capacity of forests and land use",""],[1,"18","1","Low-Carbon Infrastructure Preparation for Renewable Energy and Electric Vehicles","The public sector must therefore progress to prepare the country's infrastructure to adequately and properly accommodate a low-carbon transition to renewable energy and electric vehicles.",""],[1,"18","3","Circular Economy Promotion Measures","the starting point of economic and social development in conjunction with the preservation of environmental balance in order to preserve the health of natural resources and environment and pass them on to the future generations in the long run can be achieved by promoting the circular economy with efficient and sustainable use of resources in tune with the carrying capacity of the ecosystem by: using scientific knowhow, technology and innovation to drive the Thai economy and society towards the most efficient use of resources by all sectors; providing measures to support investments in green technology and innovation; advocating the manufacturing sector to remodel its business operations to be in line with the circular economy approach in a low-carbon society; and encouraging local communities and farmers to participate in natural resources restoration while providing them with opportunities to enjoy tangible benefits from the circular economy so as to motivate them to change their economic behaviors and adopt sustainable modes of living.",""],[1,"22","6","Production and Consumption Sustainability Transition","Ensuring the transition of production and consumption towards sustainability: Reducing pollution together with improving natural resource utilization in line with ecosystem capacity.",""],[1,"22","6","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Pathway","Pushing for a reduction of greenhouse gas emissions for Thailand to achieve carbon neutrality by 2050 and net zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2065.",""],[1,"48","3","Domestic Disposal and Reuse Strategy for Used Vehicles and Parts","Exploring and determining directions for domestic disposal of used vehicles and parts in line with the global automobile trends, as well as promoting reuse in accordance with circular economy principles.",""],[1,"49","1","CO2 Capture Technology Development","Developing CO2 capture technology, taking into consideration a product's entire lifecycle, and promoting technologies related to EV conversion as well as knowledge and technology transfer to local EV businesses.",""],[1,"62","4","Climate-Friendly Sustainable Growth Investment","Sustainable growth focusing on reducing GHG emissions, creating sustainable growth on the basis of natural resources and the environment, and making climate-friendly investments in the development of public and private infrastructure.",""],[1,"66","7","BCG-Based Industrial, Service, and Logistics Restructuring","Sub-strategy 3.2 Restructuring the industrial, service and logistics sectors to adopt BCG (Bio-Circular-Green Economy Model) framework, as well as supporting clean energy usage, reusing and recycling of factors of production, and CO2 emission reductions.",""],[1,"69","2","Eco-Friendly Growth and Low-Carbon Development","Eco- friendly development and growth by developing sustainable growth in an eco-friendly society through the use of technological advancement in business operations and daily life as well as in reducing GHG emissions and creating a low-carbon society",""],[1,"98","7","Eco-Friendly Infrastructure Investment Support","supporting investments in eco-friendly infrastructure projects, developing and applying innovation and technology to reduce pollution and environmental impacts.",""],[1,"101","1","Circular Economy Efficiency Tools and Knowledge Development","Developing tools and mechanisms as well as research and knowledge to increase efficiency in the circular use of materials so as to boost productivity and add value to the circular economy.",""],[1,"101","2","Extended Producer Responsibility Policy Framework","Implementing the Extended Producer Responsibility policy framework.",""],[1,"101","2","Private Sector Investment Support for Efficient Manufacturing and Services","Encouraging private sector investments to raise the efficiency of manufacturing processes and services with a specific aim to reduce, reuse, recycle, and minimize waste in manufacturing and service processes.",""],[1,"101","2","Green Energy Adoption and Low-Carbon Production Incentives","Stimulating the use of green energy.",""],[1,"101","2","Support Mechanisms for Lower-Carbon Production Methods","Promoting support mechanisms and incentives in adjusting production methods to enable lower carbon emissions.",""],[1,"101","4","Standard Certification System for Products and Services","Sub-strategy 1.4 Developing a standard certification system for products and services.",""],[1,"101","5","Government-Private Collaborative Mechanisms for Green Finance","Constructing collaborative mechanisms between the government and private sector.",""],[1,"101","5","Green Financial Measures and Eco-Friendly Investment Promotion","Promoting green financial measures and investments as well as sustainability reporting standards, sustainability accounting standards, as well as investments in eco-friendly economic activities.",""],[1,"103","2","Technological R&D Platforms for Circular Economy and Low-Carbon Transition","Promoting technological research and development of platforms to support businesses in the circular economy and a low-carbon society.",""],[1,"103","3","Private-Public Support for Circular Economy Business Models","Adopting private-public participation principles to support businesses to transition to circular economy business models.",""],[1,"103","3","Circular Product and Sharing Business Model Promotion","Creating new businesses with products and services designed to be long-lasting and use recyclable materials, and for-hire or pay-as-you-go business models to promote resource sharing.",""],[1,"103","4","Technology and Innovation for Resource Circularity and Waste Upcycling","Encouraging technology and innovation in mono- material packaging, second use, and upcycling for more extensive production and use.",""],[1,"103","7","Circular Economy and Low-Carbon Regulatory Reform","Revising laws to facilitate the circular economy and reduction of GHG emissions in all sectors.",""],[1,"103","7","Financial and Fiscal Incentives for Cleaner Manufacturing","Implementing financial and fiscal measures to raise the standards of manufacturing processes to reduce pollution and increase resource efficiency.",""],[1,"103","7","Circular Economy Knowledge and Standards System","Developing database systems, knowledge and guidelines on the circular economy and a low-carbon society in line with international standards.",""],[1,"103","7","Resource Efficiency and Pollution Reduction Capacity Building","Strengthening the capacity of agencies and personnel at the national, local, and community-levels in resource efficiency and pollution reduction.",""],[1,"103","7","Eco-Friendly Technology Transfer Initiative","Promoting transfers of eco- friendly technologies and innovations with low carbon emissions.",""]],"47":[[1,"101","6","Community Zero-Waste Value-Added Product Development","Encouraging communities to use garbage and agricultural residues to create new products with added value while helping them boost incomes and cut expenses.",""],[1,"101","6","Community-Business Collaboration for Circular Product Development","Instilling collaborations between local communities and businesses in using leftovers from production processes to develop products for use in the community.",""],[1,"102","2","Community-Level Garbage Reduction and Sorting Systems","Encouraging community-level garbage reduction and sorting systems as well as promoting pre-disposal garbage sorting practice for recycling, particularly as materials for community and industrial production.",""],[1,"102","2","Waste-to-Energy Conversion Support","Supporting conversions of municipal waste and leftovers from production processes into energy.",""],[1,"102","2","Model Community Circular Economy Innovation Initiative","Pushing for model communities with the capability for generating income from converting sorted garbage into products with locally appropriate innovation and technology.",""],[1,"102","3","Circular Economy Learning Communities","Encouraging the setting up of model communities based on the circular economy that corresponds with local lifestyles and knowledge, as well as transferring knowledge and lessons learned to other communities to sustainably improve their quality of life and expand community networks.",""],[1,"104","2","Consumer Incentive Mechanisms for Sustainable Consumption","Developing mechanism and tools - economic and otherwise - to incentivize and encourage consumers to change their behaviors to eco-friendly lifestyles based on accurate, reliable and transparent information.",""],[1,"104","2","Eco-friendly Procurement Support Measures","Supporting practices leading to the procurement of eco-friendly products and services.",""],[1,"104","2","Household Waste and Packaging Recycling Promotion","Encouraging the recycling of household waste and discarded packaging materials.",""],[1,"104","2","Product Labeling Expansion for Sustainable Consumer Choice","Boosting product labeling, such as green labels, carbon footprint labels, and energy labels to facilitate consumers' decision making.",""],[1,"104","3","Sharing Economy Regulation and Platform Development","Determining rules, regulations and laws to promote and regulate sharing economy businesses.",""],[1,"104","3","Collaborative Manufacturer-Consumer Network","Developing a collaborative network between manufacturers and consumers.",""],[1,"104","3","Circular Goods Exchange Platform","Building a platform to connect service users and service providers for the purpose of trade and exchange of goods and products to ensure circularity and resource efficiency.",""],[1,"104","6","Local Wisdom and Culture Promotion for Circular Economy","Sub-strategy 5.6 Stimulating the use of local wisdom and culture in line with circular economy approaches.",""],[1,"104","6","Community Resource Efficiency Promotion","Promoting approaches to community use of limited resources with maximum efficiency.",""],[1,"104","6","Local Wisdom-Based Product and Service Innovation Support","Supporting the use of local wisdom in creating products and services with innovation and creativity for self-reliance.",""],[1,"104","6","Local Wisdom and Culture Knowledge Transfer and Awareness Raising","Reviving, developing, and accommodating knowledge transfers to raise public awareness and understanding of the values and benefits of protecting local wisdom and culture.",""]],"48":[[1,"102","1","Carbon Market System Development","Researching and developing knowledge and databases for carbon trade, including data on measurements of carbon emissions from manufacturing and services, evaluation of carbon storage capacity in the forestry sector, and other carbon storage activities.",""],[1,"102","1","Carbon Emissions and Storage Certification System","Establishing a certification system for carbon emissions and storage in line with international standards.",""],[1,"102","1","Carbon Market Trading Facilitation","Facilitating carbon market trade for both emitters and capturers.",""],[1,"103","5","Carbon Capture, Utilization and Storage Technology Promotion","Promoting carbon capture, utilization and storage technology.",""]],"49":[[1,"102","6","Circular Economy Material Flow Management and Waste Recovery Platform","Analyzing material flows to efficiently manage leftovers from manufacturing and consumption and developing a circular system to make use of industrial leftovers and agricultural residues.",""],[1,"102","6","Food Loss and Waste Reduction Initiative","Reducing pre-market losses and food waste.",""],[1,"102","6","Circular Economy Business Knowledge and Innovation Platform","Developing a platform to connect circular economy businesses to knowledge and innovation, as well as revising regulations to allow recovering valuable materials from industrial waste.",""]],"50":[[1,"104","5","Eco-Friendly Public Transport Network Development","Developing an eco-friendly public transport networks with low carbon emissions and countrywide coverage.",""],[1,"104","5","Mass Transit Promotion","Promoting the use of mass transit systems.",""],[1,"104","5","Clean-Energy Vehicle Manufacturing and Adoption Support","Supporting the manufacturing and use of efficient clean-energy vehicles.",""]],"51":[[1,"18","4","Disaster Risk Prevention and Climate Resilience Measures","This can be achieved through the promotion of preventive measures against disasters in key areas, such as integrating relevant data for creating risk assessment maps in tandem with city planning; promoting the use of technology in risk management for natural disasters and climate change; educating the public and establishing participatory processes regarding disaster risk management; restoring and rehabilitating natural resources and ecosystems; and promoting international cooperation to collaboratively manage the risks of natural disasters and environmental challenges.",""],[1,"22","7","Preparedness for Ageing, Climate, Epidemics, and Cyber Threats","Promoting preparedness for coping with and seizing opportunities arising from an ageing society, climate change, epidemics, and cyber threats.",""],[1,"69","2","Human Capital, Tools, and Big Data for National Security Preparedness","Security with the goal of preparing and developing human capital, related tools and technology as well as Big Data technology to be ready to address all forms of threats, together with preventing and addressing existing and future national security problems",""],[1,"106","8","National Security Industry for Disaster Management","which aims to promote the development of an industry related to disaster management; for instance, a warning system, responsive disaster preparation, and assistance before and after disasters.",""],[1,"107","1","Climate-Friendly Sustainable Growth Strategy","which is achievable by forging climate-friendly sustainable growth with a focus on reducing greenhouse gas emissions and building a low-carbon society;",""],[1,"107","1","Disaster Management System Strengthening","improving the disaster management system and building coping and adaptive capacities among the population to minimize losses and damages from disasters and climate change impacts;",""],[1,"107","1","Integrated Water Disaster Management System","handling all forms of water- related disasters through a water management system for crisis conditions in order to effectively control and reduce losses and risks from water-related disasters in accordance with scientific principles, as well as enable comprehensive and timely collaboration on disaster management within the regions.",""],[1,"109","13","Effective Early Warning System","There Is an effective darty warning system (Le., having comprehensive average of key diumters, the linkage between local, national and International level, precision, timeliness, and effective access to vulnerable groupa)",""],[1,"109","32","Local Disaster Warning System Development","Developing local-level woming systems that are connected with national, disaster womning center",""],[1,"110","2","Disaster Risk Mapping and Prevention Planning","Integrating relevant data and risk maps for each type of disasters in order to formulate prevention and solution plans.",""],[1,"110","2","Community and Agency Disaster Collaboration Mechanism","Forging collaborations among locals, communities and relevant agencies.",""],[1,"110","2","Disaster Response Budget Integration and Agency Assignment","Integrating budget allocations, as well as clearly designating agencies responsible for plan implementation.",""],[1,"110","4","Application of National Catastrophe Models","Applying National Catastrophe Models for each type of natural disaster and climate change to improve solution mechanisms with designated responsible agencies in key affected areas in order to evaluate the effectiveness of preventive measures and consequently formulate appropriate action plans.",""],[1,"110","6","Early Warning Access and Data Use Improvement","Encouraging access to warning centers and utilizing early warning data systems efficiently.",""],[1,"110","8","Local Disaster and Climate Resilience Network Formation","Encouraging the setting up of networks among local administrative organizations, communities and civil society to ensure self-prevention and management of the impacts from natural disasters and climate change.",""],[1,"111","2","Natural Disaster and Climate Change Research Capacity Development","Developing and strengthening personnel and researchers as well as supporting research in the field of natural disaster and climate change to be systematic, continuous, comprehensive and applicable for local and national contexts.",""],[1,"111","3","Local-Level Disaster Early Warning System Upgrade","Developing local-level warning systems that are connected to the national disaster warning center, focusing on upgrading equipment and technology to support the current warning system and connect it with other countries.",""],[1,"111","3","ICT-Based Public Disaster Notification System","Adopting Information and Communication Technology (ICT) in sending notifications to the public to ensure efficiency, timeliness, and better access to vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"111","4","National Catastrophe Model Development Data Systems","Setting up data systems to develop National Catastrophe Models for risk and impact assessments that cover each type of natural disaster and climate change in key areas.",""]],"52":[[1,"107","1","Climate-Friendly Infrastructure Investment","promoting investment in climate-friendly infrastructure projects;",""],[1,"109","26","Disaster-Resilient Urban Planning and Land Use Measures","Promoting adoption of disaster preventive measures in key areas such as urban planning, systematic land- use allocation, setting up disaster safety zones, revising construction standards and criteria to include disaster resilience structures and systems, determining methods and guidelines for using low-lying area for water retention, butting drainage myburn according to the water plan ares developing structures with elimrubs- appropriate architecture",""],[1,"110","1","Disaster Prevention and Resilient Urban Planning Measures","Promoting the adoption of disaster preventive measures in key areas, such as urban planning, systematic land-use allocation, as well as setting up disaster safety zones.",""],[1,"110","1","Disaster-Resilient Construction Standards Revision","Revising construction standards and criteria to include disaster resilience structures and systems.",""],[1,"110","1","Water Retention and Climate-Appropriate Drainage Infrastructure","Determining methods and guidelines for using low-lying areas for water retention, and setting up drainage systems according to the water plans and developing structures with climate- appropriate architecture.",""],[1,"110","3","Risk-Reduction and Preventive Budget Allocation Review","Sub-strategy 1.3 Reviewing budget allocations by focusing on risk reduction and preventive measures rather than emergency responses and rehabilitation measures.",""]],"53":[[1,"109","18","Natural Disaster and Climate Change Prevention and Mitigation Funds","There are funds for the prevention and mitigation of impacts from natural disaster and climate change as well.",""],[1,"109","36","Non-Structural Disaster and Climate Change Risk Management Measures","Supporting non-structural measures to manage natural disaster and climate change u.g. tuviting laws to improve efficiency, promoting incentive measures for preparedness against natural disaster & climate change, establishing insurance system and funds to prevent and mitigate impact of natural disaster & dimate change",""],[1,"110","9","Revision and Consolidation of Natural Disaster Management Laws","Supporting non-structural measures to manage natural disasters and climate change, such as revising and consolidating laws related to natural disaster management.",""],[1,"110","9","Incentive Measures for Disaster Preparedness","Promoting incentive measures for preparedness against natural disasters and climate",""],[1,"111","1","Insurance Systems, Funds, and Business Continuity Planning for Disaster and Climate Resilience","Establishing insurance systems and funds as well as formulating business continuity plans to prevent and mitigate the impacts of natural disasters and climate change.",""]],"54":[[1,"103","6","International Technology Collaboration Network","Setting up an international collaboration network to promote the sharing, exchange and development of knowledge on policies, science, technologies, innovations, research and applications.",""],[1,"111","10","International Collaborative Mechanisms for Disaster and Climate Cooperation","Developing international collaborative mechanisms for natural disaster and climate change management and transboundary environmental impact issues, such as water management in the Mekong River basin, haze pollution from forest fires both at the bilateral and multilateral levels through signing memoranda of understanding.",""],[1,"111","10","Technical Cooperation on Disaster Risk Reduction","Moreover, building technical cooperation on disaster risk reduction with neighboring countries, and collaboratively developing technologies and innovations.",""],[1,"112","1","International Knowledge Sharing on Disaster and Climate Obligations","Sharing experiences and knowledge on international obligations related to natural disasters and climate change.",""]],"55":[[1,"67","1","Personnel Development System and Curriculum Reform","Revising personnel development systems and curricula to meet the needs of the labor market and businesses by allowing the private sector to participate in curriculum development and share expenses incurred.",""],[1,"67","1","Digital Pedagogy for Self-Learning and Business Skills","Digitalizing pedagogical methodologies to facilitate self-learning and knowledge usage in income generation and business building.",""],[1,"67","1","International Standards Upgrade for Labor Skills and Teaching","Raising labor skills and teaching levels at Thai educational institutions to international standards or the same level as those of leading global institutions to ensure the usefulness of skills in professional life.",""],[1,"74","2","Workforce Development for Future Technological Industries","Sub-strategy 4.2 Developing the workforce to support future technological shifts among enterprises in different industries and services, including the local smart electronics industry and digital industry and services.",""],[1,"74","2","Skills Alignment for Future Industries and Services","Equipping workers with skills in line with the needs of future industries and services.",""],[1,"74","2","Curriculum Improvement through Public-Private-Academic Collaboration","Improving educational curricula through collaborations between the public, private and academic sectors (domestic and international).",""],[1,"74","2","Labor Skills Enhancement and Professional Standards Development","Accelerating labor skills enhancement while developing professional standards for workers in technology-related industries.",""],[1,"74","2","Foreign Talent Attraction for Technology Skill Shortages","Attracting foreign personnel in areas of shortages such as software development and disruptive technology.",""]],"56":[[1,"113","2","Human Capital Development through Education Quality Improvement","Efforts have been made in the development of human capital in all age groups by improving the quality of all levels of education, which includes raising standards, enhancing educational processes, adopting teaching technologies and innovations, as well as developing education innovation areas - education sandboxes -with increased independence and social responsibility.",""],[1,"113","2","Expansion of Vocational and Higher Education through Development Partnerships","The role of development partners in educational programs and learning has also been promoted, particularly in providing vocational and higher education in diverse forms, such as dual vocational and co-operative education.",""],[1,"113","2","Equitable Education Fund Support for Marginalized Learners","Efforts have also been directed towards the reduction of educational disparities by identifying and providing support to marginalized children and learners through the Equitable Education Fund (EEF).",""],[1,"117","28","Primary Education Learning and Competency Development","Equipping learners at the primary education level with self-recognition, digital, skill, and necessary competencies for learning, living and working by (1) Developing new approaches to learning with practical application for self-management, communication skills, teamwork ability, high-level thinking; (2) Raising standards of vocational education; (3) Elevating qualitative & quantitative standards of teachers' education & development; (4) Improving learning evaluation system to become more reflective of students' diverse learning growth; (5) Developing learning support systems; (6) Strengthening population's morality and ethics",""],[1,"117","33","Flexible and Diverse Learning Plans for Non-Attending Learners","Developing learning alternatives for those who cannot attend formal education through compiling information and promoting flexible and diverse leaming plans for target individuals or groups",""],[1,"118","7","New Learning Approaches Pilot Programme","Developing new approaches to learning with practical implementation to ensure self-management, communication skills, teamwork capability, and high-order thinking together with proactive learning.",""],[1,"118","9","Teacher Education and Development Enhancement Programme","Elevating the qualitative and quantitative standards of teachers' education and development by planning on a number of teachers needed for each field, developing curricula to equip teachers with academic knowledge, learning management skills, the ability to use technology and innovation through online platforms.",""],[1,"118","10","Learning Evaluation System Improvement","Improving the learning evaluation system to become more reflective of students' diverse learning needs and in line with the development of personalized education so as to facilitate students' future careers.",""],[1,"119","1","Learning Support Systems Development","Developing learning support systems through (1) addressing learning loss in school age by developing practices and support systems in educational institutions, as well as promoting mixed and home-based learning programs during emergency situations; (2) increasing the efficiency of counseling systems by training teachers and counselors to help learners plan their learning as well as professional and life journey based on individual interests and aptitudes; (3) making educational institutions a safe space for all learners in both actual and virtual societies by developing appropriate physical infrastructure suitable for learning; building knowledge and understanding among teachers, educational personnel and learners of a harmonious environment based on the respect of diversity in terms of opinions and identities; promoting life-skills learning at school; and establishing welfare protection guidelines to protect learners, particularly from physical and verbal violence and bullying; (4) improving the budget and educational resources allocation system to focus on learners' development based on equality and fairness, and scaling up the coverage of technological and digital infrastructure to cover all areas; (5) decentralizing educational administrations and increasing the private sector and civil society's role in educational management by improving laws and regulations to increase independence in education management, curriculum design, budgeting and personnel management.",""]],"57":[[1,"117","26","Cross-Sectoral Workforce Development and Planning System","Developing high-capacity workforce in line with needs of target manufacturing sectors and with ability to create future jobs by [I) Promoting cross-sectoral, collaboration and linkage between education and training, co-stablishing opun, wasily accessible leaming system; (21 Formulating data system for workforce planning & development; (31 Setting measures for urgent workforce dewwkaprrunt",""],[1,"117","29","Workforce Competency Enhancement Opportunities","Boosting & distributing computuncy enhancement opportunities to all groups of workers",""],[1,"117","29","Learning-Skills-Career Entry Platform","Establishing platform that connects learning, skill curvelogement and career entry",""],[1,"117","29","Work Practice Adjustment for Technology Use","Adjusting work practices with optimal use of tuchnokagy",""],[1,"117","30","Cross-Sectoral Learning City Development","Promoting cross-sectoral development of learning cities, leaming sources and diverse creative spaces;",""],[1,"117","30","Inclusive Learning Materials Development","Creating leaming materials that leave no one behind;",""],[1,"117","30","Learning Credit Bank Development","Concretely developing leaming credit banks;",""],[1,"117","30","Lifelong Self-Learning Incentive Scheme","Offering incentives for lifelong self-lesming",""],[1,"120","3","Worker Reskilling and Upskilling Collaboration Programme","Boosting and distributing competency enhancement opportunities to all groups of workers both by reskilling and upskilling through collaborations between educational institutions, local administrative organizations, the private sector, civil society and government development agencies.",""],[1,"120","3","Foundational Short Course Development Initiative","Planning and creating short courses to forge foundational and necessary skills for life and work.",""],[1,"120","3","Flexible Skills Development Regulatory Reform","Improving rules and regulations to allow flexibility in diverse forms of implementation, especially in relation to technologies and forms of work in the future.",""],[1,"120","3","Future Skills Subsidy Credit Scheme","Introducing a subsidizing scheme as credits for acquiring future skills to every population in order for them to undertake government-certified/supported skill development courses.",""],[1,"120","4","Learning, Skills Development, and Career Entry Platforms","Establishing platforms that connect learning, skill development and career entry.",""],[1,"120","4","Responsible Agency Support for Skills Advancement","Designating responsible agencies to support those wishing to advance skills and career development.",""],[1,"120","4","Learning Recognition and Standard Certification System","Associating all forms of learning and providing standard certifications to learners.",""],[1,"120","10","Cross-Sectoral Education and Training Collaboration and Open Learning System","Promoting cross-sectoral collaborations and linkages between education and training as well as co-establishing an open, easily accessible learning system.",""],[1,"121","1","High-Capability Workforce Development Support Measures","Offering incentives and supportive mechanisms for training and educational programming for high-capability personnel.",""],[1,"121","1","International Knowledge and Personnel Exchange Mechanism","Advocating for knowledge and personnel exchanges through international cooperation mechanisms to assist in the development of a high-capability workforce in line with the country's development direction.",""],[1,"121","2","Workforce Planning Information Systems Development","Developing information systems for workforce planning and development, including collecting data on workforce demands and supplies and identifying in-demand competencies throughout the supply and value chains for each of the target manufacturing and service industries.",""],[1,"121","3","Urgent Workforce Development Pilot Programs","Establishing measures for urgent workforce development by piloting education programs areas which are deemed essential for the country's development, such as artificial intelligence and data analysis.",""],[1,"122","3","Learning Credit Bank Development","Concretely developing learning credit banks to connect all levels and all classes of learning in basic, vocational, formal, non-formal and informal educations, ranging from the secondary, vocational to higher levels, to ensure agility and diverse learning options to all levels of learners.",""],[1,"122","4","Lifelong Self-Learning Incentives","Offering incentives for lifelong self-learning through providing funds and training credits for all groups of population, as well as training privileges for learning facility visits.",""],[1,"122","4","Private Sector Educational Innovation CSR Incentives","Encouraging the private sector in the field of educational innovation production to offer product usage free of charge as a corporate social responsibility activity.",""],[1,"122","5","Flexible and Diverse Learning Alternatives Development","Compiling educational information and promoting flexible and diverse learning plans for target individuals or groups to allow them to plan their learning based on personal goals and undertake skills recognition.",""]],"58":[[1,"117","31","National Mechanism to Attract High-Capacity Workers","Establishing rutional mechanism tu embrace high-capacity workers; (2) Promoting importation of highly- skilled foreign experts",""],[1,"120","10","Supportive Environment for High-Capability Personnel","Developing and enhancing a supportive environment to attract and retain high-capability personnel who possess",""],[1,"121","5","National High-Capacity Workforce Attraction and Retention Mechanism","Establishing a national mechanism to embrace high-capacity workers, both Thais and foreign nationals born in Thailand, and encourage them to use their capacities to serve in the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"121","6","Incentives to Attract Highly Skilled Foreign Experts","Promoting the import of highly skilled foreign experts through incentives to attract foreign experts to settle in the country and work in the field of technology and innovation.",""],[1,"121","6","Retention Incentives for Foreign Graduates","Incentivizing locally graduated foreign students to remain in the country to take part in innovation development.",""]],"59":[[1,"31","8","Agricultural Infrastructure and Management System Development","To develop infrastructure and management system to ensure quality, food security, and sustainability of the agricultural sector",""],[1,"31","40","Agricultural Business Unit Support for Farm Management Efficiency","Promoting the role of agricultural, instituciones an agricultural business units in Improving farm management efficiency, post harvest activities and delivery to customers to cut costs and Increase farm procluce's value",""],[1,"31","40","Farm Product Collection and Transport Infrastructure Development","7.2 Developing bule Infrastructure and facilities to collect and tramport farm products to link outputs throughout the faim product supply chain",""],[1,"31","40","Farm Loss Data Collection System","7.3 Developing ciata collection system for farm loss as a baseline for future ansesment",""],[1,"31","41","Systematic Land Allocation to Farmers","Promoting / supporting systematic land allocation to farmers through editing mechanisms eg. ONLB & ALHO",""],[1,"31","41","Protection of High-Potential Agricultural Land","Protecting high potendal agricultural. area and Increasing access cultivated areas for farmers.",""],[1,"31","41","Boundary Setting for Farm Use","Setting appropriate boundaries fo farm use",""],[1,"34","7","Basic Agricultural Produce Collection and Transport Infrastructure Development","Developing basic infrastructure and facilities to collect and transport agricultural produce in order to link outputs throughout the agricultural product supply chain.",""],[1,"34","8","Farm Loss Data Collection System Development","Developing data collection system for farm loss as a baseline for future assessment.",""],[1,"34","9","Systematic Land Allocation to Farmers","Promoting and supporting systematic land allocation to farmers through existing mechanisms, such as land allocation to communities as per government policies and land allocation by the Agricultural Land Reform Office.",""],[1,"34","10","Protection of High-Potential Agricultural Areas and Expansion of Cultivated Land Access","Protecting high-potential agricultural areas and increasing access to cultivated areas for farmers, as well as determining appropriate boundaries for agricultural use.",""]],"60":[[1,"31","43","Community Food Security Promotion","Promoting communhy access to food security with quantity & nutrition and diverse, safe, sufficient food reserve.",""],[1,"31","44","Farmer Knowledge and Skills Development Programme","Developing and codancing farmerd' knowledge & shils In ferm mergemert occupational health & ufety, and digital. agricultural busirwen lo elevate capability in order to become wvart Drvert 55.2",""],[1,"31","44","Agricultural Value-Adding Enterprise Support","Strengthening & enhancing capa bility of agriculturel. Initiations to operate value-adding budnost.",""],[1,"31","44","Cooperative Development Support","Ravidng cooperatives development barva & drenghun coopevelien",""],[1,"33","13","Farmer Knowledge and Skills Development for Direct Online Trade","Enhancing farmers' knowledge and skills to enable direct online trade of their produce including crops, catches and livestock.",""],[1,"34","2","Farmers' Transaction Fee Reduction for Standard Accreditation","Facilitating a reduction of farmers' transaction fees regarding standard accreditation throughout the supply chain to increase access and to incentivize farmers to produce products with higher standards.",""],[1,"34","6","Strengthening Agricultural Institutions as Business Units","Promoting the role of agricultural institutions (cooperatives/farmers' collectives/social enterprises) as agricultural business units in improving farm management efficiency, post-harvest activities and delivery to customers so as to reduce costs and increase the values of farm produce.",""],[1,"35","3","Community Food Security Reserve Model Promotion","The food security reserve model for community should be encouraged to establish as a role model for further implementation.",""],[1,"35","5","Farmer Knowledge and Skills Development for Smart Farming","Sub-strategy 11.1 Developing and extending farmers' knowledge and skills in farm management, occupational health and safety, and digital agricultural business to elevate farmers' capability in order to become smart farmers.",""],[1,"35","6","Agricultural Cooperative and Community Enterprise Value-Addition Support","Sub-strategy 11.2 Strengthening and enhancing capability of agricultural cooperatives, farmers' collectives and community enterprises to operate value-adding businesses.",""]],"61":[[1,"32","1","Targeted Agricultural R&D for Technology and Innovation","Supporting targeted research and development of technology and innovation in agricultural production in collaboration with private sector to apply in particular market appropriately.",""],[1,"32","2","Technology and Innovation Research Application Promotion","Promoting and implementing the application of technology and innovation research, conducted by research institutes, universities and vocational schools, the private sector, and agricultural organizations, to ensure the beneficial use of research and participation of both technology developers and users.",""],[1,"32","4","Agricultural Processing GDP Data Development","Moreover, gross domestic product (GDP) data on agricultural processing product should be developed for formulating further support.",""],[1,"32","6","Farmer Innovation and Agricultural Data Utilization Support","Encouraging farmers to utilize diverse information, such as scientific knowledge, technology and innovation in the production process, agricultural database and local identity in analyzing, planning and improving products, productivity and agricultural processing.",""],[1,"33","3","Continuous Collection of Agricultural Input and Output Data","The data on output volumes and use of biological substances should be continuously collected for further suitable measures.",""],[1,"33","12","Continuous Agricultural Commodity Price Data Collection","Encouraging continuous data collection on price of agricultural commodities regarding the different market location to compare the price between regional and central markets.",""],[1,"34","11","Connected Agricultural Data Repository","Developing a connected agricultural data repository with public access to be adopted as a basis for boosting the efficiency of agricultural production and value- add creation.",""],[1,"35","2","Agricultural Data Platform and Application Development","Sub-strategy 9.2 Developing platforms and applications for accessing data repositories to allow the use of agriculture-related data in classifying farmers' production patterns and capability.",""]],"62":[[1,"28","4","Agricultural Competitiveness and Value-Addition Enhancement","Competitiveness enhancement with the following goals: 1) Thailand becomes a developed country with stable and sustainable economic growth; and 2) Thailand's national competitiveness is increased as per the National Strategy's master plan on agriculture, which focuses on raising manufacturing safety standards, leveraging the outstanding and unique quality of Thailand's agricultural produce and biological diversity to add value to agricultural produce, and using modern technology and innovation in production and farm management.",""],[1,"31","7","Agricultural Value-Addition Promotion","To increase value added of agricultural produce and processed agricultural products",""],[1,"32","3","High-Value Agricultural Production and Market Expansion Strategy","Encouraging the production and market expansion of high-value agricultural produce and processed agricultural products such as safety-guaranteed produce, herbal extracts, medical food, alternative foods, functional foods, bioenergy, biomaterials and biochemicals, and plant-based and insect-based proteins:",""],[1,"32","9","Government Procurement of Quality Agricultural Produce","Encouraging government agencies to consume quality agricultural produce and processed agricultural products such as agricultural produce for hospital, school and prison use, as well as medical food.",""]],"64":[[1,"31","45","Agricultural Collaborative Mechanisms and Partnerships","12.1 Supporting agriculturel. argentiora /'counch\" role in collaborative mechanibms amony public agencies, private & academic actors in eoch province lo buld wquilabi wcomomile pautrenchipe in line with roko, dulko and wspomsibilka",""],[1,"31","45","Private Sector and Farmer Agricultural Partnership Promotion","12.2 Promoting priebe actor's role as economic partner with agricultural irettutora & farmercin diverse budireu formatrio collaboral.Jwwly Bocal. efficiency of production process with appropriate",""],[1,"34","3","Private Sector Linkage for Certified Agricultural Produce Supply Chains","Encouraging the private sector's role in linking certified agricultural produce to the value-added agricultural product supply chain.",""],[1,"35","6","Local Private Sector and Education Institution Support for Agricultural Business Scaling","Supporting the role of local private sector and educational institutions, including vocational schools and higher education institutions as a service provider, technology transfers, and business consultants so as to enable effective adaptation and scaling up of agricultural businesses.",""],[1,"35","7","Review and Revise Cooperative-Related Laws and Regulations","Sub-strategy 11.3 Reviewing and revising cooperative-related laws and regulations to keep up with current trends while strengthening cooperatives, such as revising accounting systems and financial auditing to improve speed, transparency and independence in order to prevent and address problems in a timely manner as well as to build public confidence in the cooperative system.",""],[1,"35","8","Provincial Agricultural Collaboration Mechanisms","Supporting the role of agricultural organizations/councils in collaborative mechanisms among government agencies and the private and academic sectors in each province to ensure that the production and business operations of farmers in particular areas are in line with those areas' potentials, the private sector's needs, provincial government agencies' missions, and the expertise of local educational institutions.",""],[1,"35","9","Private Sector Partnership in Agricultural Business Promotion","Sub-strategy 12.2 Promoting the role of the private sector as an economic partner in agricultural businesses with agricultural institutions and individual farmers to foster",""]],"65":[[1,"38","1","Tourism Regulatory Reform and Digital Promotion","obsolete/obstructive laws and regulations as well as the use of technology and data to efficiently develop and promote tourism.",""],[1,"39","23","Review and Revision of Outdated Business Regulations and Procedures","Reviewing & revising outdated laws, regulations and procedures which impede business operations and license application of small enterprises",""],[1,"39","29","Review and Revise Public Procurement Regulations","Reviewing & revising laws and regulations related to 6.1 government budget & public procurement to fadtrate private sector engagement In Investment & development of tourist destinations in colaboration with communities and the public sect enabling public procurement of products & services from local communit with proper environmental, sufsty & hygiene standards.",""],[1,"39","37","Regulatory Simplification for Business Operations","Eliminating outdated legal constraints and regulation obstructing business operations",""],[1,"39","37","Technology-Enabled Licensing for Tourism and Small Businesses","liansing of tourism related businesses, through technology exploitation, particularly foraccommodation and related business and small businesses.",""],[1,"39","37","Business Registration Facilitation and Legal Framework Integration","Providing ease of process to encourage entrepreneurs to register and join the legal framework government database.",""],[1,"39","37","Strengthened Enforcement of Business Regulations","Ensuring strict, efficient and unbizet enforcement of relavant guidelines and laws togather witk ctors.",""],[1,"39","43","Environmental Responsibility Law Reform for Large Businesses","revising laws to encourage environmental responsibility fic68 Developing a large businesses.",""],[1,"39","44","Review and Revise Laws and Regulations for Tourism Technology","Reviewing & revising lavs and regulations which obstruct the tourism technology ag.",""],[1,"41","8","Review and Revision of Outdated Business and Licensing Regulations","Strategy 5 Reviewing and revising outdated laws, regulations and procedures which impede business operations and license application of small enterprises to encourage a transition towards sustainable high-quality tourism:",""],[1,"41","9","Budget and Public Procurement Regulatory Reform for Tourism Investment","Reviewing and revising laws and regulations related to government budget and public procurement to facilitate private sector engagement in the investment and development of tourist destinations in collaboration with communities and the public sector.",""],[1,"41","9","Local Community Procurement Standards for Public Purchasing","Enabling public procurement of products and services from local communities with appropriate environmental, safety, and hygienic standards.",""],[1,"42","1","Tourism Business Regulatory Simplification and Legal Registration Support","Eliminating outdated legal constraints and regulations obstructing business operations and licensing of tourism-related businesses through technology exploitation, in particular for accommodation and related businesses with an emphasis on covering small businesses.",""],[1,"42","1","Tourism Business Registration and Database Integration Facilitation","Providing ease of process to encourage small entrepreneurs to register and join the legal framework and government database to enable them to link with high-quality tourism.",""],[1,"42","1","Tourism Law Enforcement and Environmental Responsibility Reform","Ensuring strict, efficient and unbiased enforcement of relevant guidelines and laws together with revising laws to encourage environmental responsibility from tourism-related businesses.",""],[1,"42","2","Review and Revision of Tourism Technology Regulations","Sub-strategy 5.3 Reviewing and revising laws and regulations which obstruct tourism technology, particularly in relation to online travel agencies and sharing economy platforms to increase compliance, convenience, and safety for tourists and surrounding communities as well as to facilitate future development.",""]],"66":[[1,"39","24","Smart Tourism Information System Upgrade","Upgrading tourism information system to smart tourism system to facilitate access & use by tourists, businesses and government agencies",""],[1,"39","30","Tourism Data Collection System Harmonization","Harmonizing in-depth for tourism data collection system business for consistency, reliability and recentness to enable its use by enterprises operations and by government Sgancias in policymaking on effective tourism development .",""],[1,"39","33","Community Development Program Monitoring Systems","Encouraging development of monitoring systems to overseef 2 Supporting linkages community development program Implementation by al sectors",""],[1,"39","38","Tourism Digital Integration and Central E-Application Development","between public and private sector databases using private sector-developed applications, such as the TAT's TAGTHAL, to connect platforms and ensure ease of travel.",""],[1,"41","9","Community Development Program Monitoring Systems","Encouraging the development of monitoring systems to oversee the implementation of community development programs by all sectors, including the public, private, academic sectors and civil society, to eliminate redundancy and ensure development efficiency and continuity.",""],[1,"42","3","Tourism Data Collection System Harmonization","Harmonizing the in-depth tourism data collection system for consistency, reliability and recentness to enable its use by enterprises for business operations and by government agencies in policymaking regarding effective tourism development.",""],[1,"42","4","Government-Private Tourism Data Linkage Platform","Supporting linkages between government and private sector databases using private sector-developed applications, such as TAGTHAI, to connect platforms and ensure ease of travel for tourists especially by providing useful information on visa, immigration, VAT refunds, emergency warnings, etc., and to further develop a central application platform for Thailand's tourism industry with a large central database open to all sectors to facilitate tourist behavior analysis.",""],[1,"42","4","National Tourism Platform Development","Pressing for the development of a national tourism platform.",""],[1,"42","5","Large-Scale Tourism Database Development","Developing a large-scale tourism database integrating all partner agencies, including the Tourism Authority of Thailand, Tourism Council of Thailand and Board of Trade of Thailand, which enables the public and diverse business sectors to mutually establish a cross-sectoral in-depth knowledge base which allows an effective use of data to search, study, analyze, understand, plan and conduct marketing activities to reach high-potential customers.",""]],"67":[[1,"39","41","Thailand Tourism Promotion Fund","collection for the \"Thailand Tourism Pro mo tio rFund\" as a circulating capital to develop tourism, boost competitiveness, build community skills in management, marketing and conservation of tourism - related resources.",""],[1,"39","41","Foreign Tourist Insurance Scheme","Providing insurance for foreign tourists while travelling in the country.",""],[1,"41","3","Tourism Fee Collection for Tourism Promotion Fund","Advocating for the collection of tourism fees to contribute to the \"Thailand's Tourism Promotion Fund\" as a circulating capital to develop tourism, increase competitiveness, build community skills in management, marketing and conservation of tourism- related resources, as well as provide insurance for foreign tourists while travelling in the country.",""]],"68":[[1,"54","31","Medical Fee Regulation and Management Mechanism","Establishing mechanism to regulate and manage medical fees",""],[1,"54","34","Medical and Wellness Hub Regulatory Reform","Revising regulations to facilitate medical & wellness hub initiative",""],[1,"55","4","Review and Revise Laws and Regulations for the Medical and Wellness Hub Initiative","Reviewing/revising relevant laws and regulations to facilitate the medical and wellness hub initiative.",""],[1,"55","5","Medical and Wellness Hub Legal and Regulatory Support","Exploring the feasibility of a specific law supporting the medical and wellness hub initiative that addresses operational constraints, such as a law related to digital medicine, use of foreign healthcare coverage and social welfare system, and immigration.",""],[1,"55","6","Single License for Wellness and Medical Services","Revising relevant laws to combine licenses for wellness and medical services into a single license that covers all activities related to wellness facilities, hospitals and hotels, together with revising relevant laws to facilitate professionals in wellness-related fields that are not yet being taught in Thailand, such as nature therapy, to provide medical supports under their professional licenses.",""],[1,"58","6","Medical Fee Regulation Mechanism","Developing mechanisms and guidelines to regulate medical fees, which might be affected by the medical hub policy, to ensure appropriate costs.",""],[1,"58","6","Health Security Payment System Expansion","Improving the health security payment system to become more comprehensive so as to allow people to access necessary medical services in an inclusive and fair manner.",""]],"69":[[1,"55","2","Medical Tourism Partnership Promotion","Encouraging connections with business partners organizing medical services in Thailand for foreign patients, especially those from countries where the health security system covers medical expenses incurred in Thailand.",""],[1,"55","8","Comprehensive Wellness City Development","Incorporating Thailand's distinguished identity into wellness services by encouraging all local sectors to collaboratively create a comprehensive wellness city, leveraging local knowledge in traditional Thai medicine, alternative medicine and health tourism in local communities to develop Thai brands of wellness services and products with international competitiveness.",""],[1,"55","9","World-Class Wellness Services Manager Development and Overseas Expansion Investment","Pressing for the development of world-class managers in wellness services to build the reputation of advanced wellness services for foreigners as well as making a joint investment to expand services abroad, which might result in an increase in uptakes at low- and mid-level.",""],[1,"55","10","Quality Standards for Wellness Facilities and Businesses","Developing professional standards of wellness-related businesses through quality management processes.",""],[1,"55","10","SME Registration Incentives for Health Businesses","Offering incentives for SMEs to register under the Health Business",""],[1,"56","2","Consumer Behavior Study for Service Uptake","Studying consumer behaviors in each age and ethnicity group to identify incentives for service uptakes.",""]],"70":[[1,"56","4","Medical Technology Evaluation and Product Testing Standards System","Developing a system for the evaluation of medical technology and medical product testing standards so as to meet international standards, such as scholarly articles on safety standards for product registrations in Asian, US, and European markets, to ensure convenience and universal standard in product testing, as well as to create opportunities for Thailand to undertake research, analysis and accreditation of foreign products.",""],[1,"56","5","Testing Center Upgrading and Biosafety Laboratory Expansion","Collaborating with the private sector to develop and upgrade comprehensive testing centers to achieve international standards for medical products, including prototyping centers, laboratory animal centers, and centers for clinical trials in humans.",""],[1,"56","6","Biopharmaceutical and Vaccine Pilot Plant Development Support","Developing production bases and supporting the setting up of pilot plants for biopharmaceuticals, drugs, herbal products and vaccines with international standards, particularly vaccines against emerging and re-emerging diseases, so as to meet domestic needs, minimize imports, and ensure the long-term security of the public health system.",""],[1,"56","7","Health Products Regulatory System Reform","Sub-strategy 3.2 Reforming the regulatory system for health products.",""],[1,"56","8","Joint Investment Support for Domestic Health Product Production","Revising relevant laws, regulations and measures on joint investment between the government and SMEs to facilitate domestic production.",""],[1,"56","8","Tax Incentives for Health and Medical Product Investment","Utilizing tax mechanisms to promote investment.",""],[1,"56","8","Standards-Based Manufacturing Support for Health Products","Supporting the manufacturing of products with international standards and market demands with a focus on traceability of raw materials.",""],[1,"56","8","Scientific Evidence and Supply Chain Confidence Initiative","Building confidence through scientific evidences in products throughout the supply chain.",""],[1,"56","8","Digital Health Product Market Platform","Establishing a digital platform to connect demand and supply while marketing products domestically and internationally.",""],[1,"57","1","List of Thai Innovations and Public Procurement Reform","Improving the List of Thai Innovations for ease of use and facilitate the development of the healthcare industry with strict and serious enforcement in the public sector.",""],[1,"57","2","Tax Incentives for Domestic Medical Equipment Procurement","Forging attitudes and encouraging private healthcare facilities and medical schools to use domestically produced medical equipment which are of high quality, safe, efficient, and cost-effective by offering tax benefits for the procurement of Thailand-produced medical equipment.",""],[1,"57","2","Medical School Curriculum Inclusion of Domestic Medical Equipment Standards","Enforcing the inclusion of a list of Thailand-produced medical equipment with international standards in medical school curricula and service systems.",""]],"71":[[1,"15","3","Economic and Urban Development Dissemination Initiative","These can be achieved by the dissemination of economic and urban development to distribute benefits from economic progress, provide equal opportunities to access basic infrastructure and quality public services, enhance physical, logistical and digital infrastructure to accommodate economic and urban development so that all groups of people can access and benefit from technology, including access to knowledge, finance, and social welfare.",""],[1,"15","3","Inclusive Education and Skills Development for Poor Children and Youth","This can be achieved by promoting quality education and professional skill development to children and youth from the poor household group along with developing comprehensive and inclusive social security and protection that are systematically integrated to ensure stability in life and adequate social protection for all to be free from poverty in a sustainable manner.",""],[1,"15","3","Integrated Social Security and Protection System","This can be achieved by promoting quality education and professional skill development to children and youth from the poor household group along with developing comprehensive and inclusive social security and protection that are systematically integrated to ensure stability in life and adequate social protection for all to be free from poverty in a sustainable manner.",""]],"72":[[1,"66","8","Electronic Transactions and Personal Data Protection Law Development","Developing effective laws on electronic transactions and personal data protection.",""],[1,"71","9","Public Digital Dashboard for Government Service Transactions","There & public digtal dashboard to track the digital transactions of govemment services by 2023, and all goverment services are digitaod by 2027",""],[1,"71","23","Digital Government Services and Platforms Development","Developing digital services and platforms to support the digital transformation of government administration into a fully digital government",""],[1,"71","34","International Data Access Standards and Interagency Data Exchange Framework","Developing internationally accepted standards & rules for accessing data from smart gadgets and supporting exchange & linkage of data among public agencies and with local & regional private sectors",""],[1,"71","42","Cybersecurity Risk Management System Development","Pruning for development of cybersecurity risk management system to protect Thailand- developed technology & platforms",""],[1,"72","1","Digital Government Transformation and E-Government Platform Development","Developing digital services and platforms to support the digital transformation of government administration into e-government, a fully digital government, by encouraging government agencies to use technology and digital devices to perform duties, including online systems for clerical works, e-payments, cloud storage, electronic services, and transactions for clients as well as full data integration and connection across all government agencies.",""],[1,"73","2","International Data Access Standards and Rules","Developing internationally accepted standards and rules for accessing data from smart gadgets.",""],[1,"73","2","Government Data Exchange and Linkage Platform","Supporting the exchange and linkage of data among government agencies and with local and regional private sectors to build big data for research and development of relevant products and services.",""],[1,"74","3","Digital Economy and Consumer Protection Legal Reform","Pressing for and revising relevant laws to promote a digital economy and consumer protection.",""],[1,"74","3","Copyright Law Enforcement","Strictly enforcing copyright laws as well as pressing for e- waste management laws and regulations.",""],[1,"74","3","Regulatory Reform to Remove Barriers to Digital Investment","Developing and revising government regulations which hinder investments, recruitment of highly skilled labor, adoption of technology and digital innovation, and overall growth of the digital industry and services.",""],[1,"74","3","Technology Transfer Requirements in Public Procurement","Mandating technology transfers as a condition for large-scale public procurements to boost the domestic production of infrastructure components.",""],[1,"74","3","Digital Services Monitoring and Taxation System","Establishing a system to monitor and regulate digital services, particularly transactions on foreign platforms, for the purpose of taxation.",""],[1,"74","5","Cybersecurity Risk Management and Data Sovereignty Policy Framework","Pressing for the development of cybersecurity risk management systems in accordance with international principles together with data sovereignty policies to protect Thailand-developed technologies and platforms by formulating rules and conditions related to data sovereignty.",""]],"73":[[1,"71","30","Enterprise Brand Development and Export Promotion for Smart Devices","Encouraging enterprises to develop their own brands and boost exports of smart dechical, appliances & dechionic gadgets",""],[1,"71","35","E-commerce Software and Digital Content Development","Promoting e-commerce software and digital contents development that creatively incorporate Thai culture lifestyles & tourist destinations etc.",""],[1,"72","7","Enterprise Branding and Smart Electronics Export Promotion","Encouraging enterprises to develop their own brands and boost exports of smart electrical appliances and electronic gadgets, focusing on foreign markets where Thailand has potentials, such as ASEAN, Europe, and the United States.",""],[1,"73","7","E-commerce Software and Digital Content Development","Promoting the development of e-commerce software and the creation of digital content that creatively incorporate Thai culture, lifestyles and tourist destinations etc. to generate economic value add in all aspects, such as virtual museums, virtual cultural performance stages, virtual concerts and virtual movie characters.",""]],"74":[[1,"71","27","Domestic Entrepreneur Technology Adoption and Smart Electronics Promotion","Promoting and developing domestic entrepreneurs to adopt technology. digital innovation as well as smart electronics in production and services to increase productivity and profitability",""],[1,"72","2","Domestic Entrepreneur Technology Adoption Support","Promoting and developing domestic entrepreneurs to adopt technology, digital innovation as well as smart electronics in production and services to increase productivity and profitability.",""],[1,"72","2","SME Smart Digital Tools Financing Support","Providing funds to support the adoption of smart electronic and digital tools, particularly by SMEs.",""],[1,"72","2","Digital Platforms for Agricultural Markets and Operators","Attaching importance to the development of digital platforms to assist agricultural markets and Thai agricultural operators in utilizing digital technology to comprehensively support the agricultural industry as well as in building preparedness for disasters and seasonal changes.",""],[1,"72","2","Smart Factory and Smart Medicine Expansion","Promoting an extension of the agricultural sector to include production, such as smart factories and smart medicine, as well as boosting service transactions on Thai digital platforms by different sectors, such as agricultural markets, tourism, medicine and wellness, and finance.",""],[1,"72","4","Promotion of Advanced Digital Technologies in Everyday Living","Promoting the use of advanced digital technologies in everyday living, including e-learning, smart gadgets and electronic transactions.",""],[1,"72","4","Social Media Threat Awareness and Fake News Resilience Skills","Raising awareness on social media threats as well as basic skills to build immunity to fake news.",""],[1,"73","8","Digital Talent Development Initiative","Attracting and developing talent to enable a great leap forward in the development of the Thai workforce and industries.",""]],"75":[[1,"75","2","Integrated SME Promotion Budgeting Framework","the government has focused on building an enabling ecosystem for businesses through integrated budgeting for SME promotion; for instance, appropriate funding, market promotion, standards, research and development and innovation by relevant agencies.",""],[1,"75","2","SME Registration and Data System","a considerable number of SMEs are informal and not listed in a proper system, resulting in the public sector's lack of clear and sufficient data on them and therefore limiting the ability to develop appropriate policies and measures to support, assist, remedy and meet the specific needs of SMEs",""],[1,"78","17","Comprehensive SME Database System","There Is a current, comprehensive SME databune system accesible to both government and SMES",""],[1,"78","21","SME Database Linkage Platform","Developing platform to link SME databases and encouraging SMEs 10 participate in system",""],[1,"78","28","One ID System for SMEs and Digital Transaction Promotion","Establishing one ID system for SMEs and encouraging SMEs' unagu in digital transactionis",""],[1,"78","32","Central SME Data Portal and E-Government Linkage","Developing a central portal to link SME data with the e- govemment platform.",""],[1,"78","35","SME Promotion Fund Financing Support","Allocating sufficient budgets for continuoin SME promotion through SME Promotion Fund",""],[1,"78","35","Integrated SME Support and Promotion Services","Supporting Office of SME Promotion (OSMEP) ma policy-making body to fully integrate SME auistance & promotion services.",""],[1,"78","41","Common Cross-Agency Monitoring and Evaluation Indicators","Adjusting monitoring & evaluation mechanisms & processes by setting common indicators across all agencies and allowing moru engagermini by representatives of SMES, private sector and acaclumia",""],[1,"79","5","Central SME Data Portal and Data Sharing Framework","Developing a central portal to link SME data with the e- government platform.",""],[1,"81","1","SME Assistance and Promotion Integration","Supporting the Office of SME Promotion (OSMEP) as a policy- making body to fully integrate SME assistance and promotion services.",""],[1,"81","2","Common Indicators and Inclusive Policy Monitoring Mechanism","Adjusting monitoring and evaluation mechanisms and processes by establishing common indicators across all agencies and allowing more engagement by representatives of SMEs, the private sector and academia to ensure co-ownership of the policies between the government, the private sector and the people.",""]],"76":[[1,"85","23","Collaborative ICT System for Area and Urban Development","Establishing ICT system for collaborative area & urban development among public & private sectors and the public",""],[1,"87","3","Collaborative Area and Urban Development ICT System","Establishing an ICT system for collaborative area and urban development among the public sector, the private sector and the public.",""],[1,"87","3","ICT Data Access Regulatory Reform","Reviewing and revising regulations that obstruct access to ICT data in order to promote collaboration among development partners.",""],[1,"87","3","Open Data Sharing for Area and Urban Planning","Supporting the disclosure and sharing of data between the public sector, private sector and the public to benefit area and urban development planning.",""],[1,"87","3","Open-Access Research and Digital Capacity Support","Supporting open-access research, innovation, data collection and processing for the purpose of area and urban management, including city data collection and management system, ICT system for local-level budgeting and project management, and digital skills enhancement.",""],[1,"87","4","Smart City Development and Disaster Preparedness Programme","Sub-strategy 2.3 Promoting the development of smart cities with change and disaster preparedness that respond to the needs of all population groups in the area.",""],[1,"87","4","Smart City Partnership and Community Collaboration Mechanism","Placing importance on smart city development with considerations of communities' traditional values in accordance with the goals of the Master Plan under the National Strategy, achievable through collaborations among the local private sector, inhabitants and civil society.",""],[1,"87","4","City Digital Preparedness and Capacity-Building Initiative","Assessing the city's digital preparedness and strengthening the capacity of cities with potentials to enable them to advance into smart cities, also by instilling appropriate knowledge and understanding of digital technology.",""],[1,"87","4","Townhall-Based Urban Planning and Technology Adoption Mechanism","Designing townhall mechanisms for collective planning on technology adoption to ensure transparent and effective urban management.",""]],"77":[[1,"88","3","Personnel, Education, Research, Technology and Innovation Development","Sub-strategy 3.2 Developing personnel, education, research, technology and innovation to achieve quality, adequacy, and adaptability to meet the needs of local target industry and services so as to continuously support the expansion of the industrial and service sectors, particularly personnel in creative economy, tourism, agriculture/bio-industry, and future industries, which require advanced technologies and innovations.",""],[1,"88","3","Multi-Stakeholder Collaboration for Research and Innovation Personnel","Encouraging collaboration among educational institutions, research institutes, the public sector and the private sector in producing research and innovation-related personnel to address local issues, develop local capacity, and design/develop products with international-level quality to meet the demands of market.",""],[1,"88","3","Farmer, Entrepreneur, SME and Startup Capability Development","Enhancing the capability of farmers, community entrepreneurs, SMEs and startups in order for them to become smart farmers and tech startups.",""],[1,"88","3","Creative Services Labor Skills Development","Developing labor skills to cater to creative services.",""]],"78":[[1,"110","6","Disaster and Climate Change Education Integration","Incorporating knowledge on disasters and climate change management into curricula at all educational levels.",""],[1,"110","6","Disaster and Climate Change Learning Centers","Establishing learning centers.",""]],"79":[[1,"109","39","Nature-Based Disaster and Climate Adaptation Measures","Supporting nature-based solutions to sustainably address natural disaster& climate change e.g. rehabilitsting wetlands for water retention and filtering of sediments to prevent flood",""],[1,"111","7","Natural Resources Conservation and Rehabilitation for Disaster and Climate Resilience","Enhancing the roles of people, communities and the private sector in natural resources conservation and rehabilitation to prevent and mitigate the impacts of natural disasters and climate change.",""],[1,"111","8","Wetland Rehabilitation for Flood Control","rehabilitating wetlands for water retention and filtering sediments to prevent floods",""],[1,"111","8","Watershed Forest Rehabilitation and Local Water Retention Systems","mitigating droughts by rehabilitating watershed forests, building small local-level water retention systems, and improving land use",""],[1,"111","8","Coastal Ecosystem Restoration for Erosion Protection","preventing coastal erosion by reviving original coastal ecosystems as natural defenses",""]],"80":[[1,"119","4","Demand-Directed Higher Education Financing Reform","Reforming higher education based on demand-directed budgeting and resource allocation directed to learners, together with developing and improving educational programming, standards, and quality assurance system.",""],[1,"119","4","Private Sector Engagement and Resource Mobilization for Education","Promoting private sector engagement and resource mobilization in educational programming.",""],[1,"119","5","Higher Education Learning Recovery and Workforce Alignment Program","Promoting higher education institutions' role in addressing learning losses due to the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"119","5","Personalized Learning and Work-Integrated Education Program","Connecting learning and working through personalized learning programs.",""],[1,"119","5","Public-Private Collaboration in Educational Programming","Building and strengthening collaborations in educational programming between the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"119","5","Education Innovation Support Initiative","Supporting innovation in education programming with advanced educational innovations to produce a workforce that meets the country's needs.",""],[1,"119","5","Higher Education Quality Improvement Initiative","Encouraging higher education institutions to raise the quality of education and personnel so as to support development with regard to social and community contexts.",""]],"81":[[1,"120","5","Flexible Work Practices and Remote Working Enablement","Adjusting work practices with optimal use of technologies to allow flexibility in working from anywhere.",""],[1,"120","5","Talent Development and Fair Workplace Promotion","Incubating an organizational culture of encouraging talents to maximize their full potentials as well as promoting fair workplaces in order to eradicate corruption and enhance the organizations' competency.",""],[1,"120","5","Workforce Rights, Safety, and Human Rights Compliance","Adhering to human rights principles, particularly labor rights, to ensure the security and safety of the workforce.",""],[1,"121","5","Borderless Remote Work Environment Support","Providing borderless work environments that accommodate remote working with leading international public and private institutions.",""],[1,"121","5","Sabbatical Leave Support for Workforce Development","Supporting sabbatical leave as a means to enhance a high-capacity workforce's knowledge and potentials.",""],[1,"121","5","Workplace Culture and Quality Workforce Environment Initiative","Creating professional culture, organizational culture and a work environment that allow a quality workforce to utilize their full potentials while staying happy at work.",""]],"82":[[1,"132","6","Local Development Participation and Community Revitalization Initiative","participating in local development activities and join forces with local administrative organizations and other local agencies to implement the 13th Plan, which in turn will help revitalize the community and encourage local communities to become the major forces in national development",""]]}});